    skos:definition """Reports providing information on the observed weather conditions at a fixed
observation station."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PRESENT WEATHER"@en .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/02064e6f-5647-4da1-bb5e-800924a82e27> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/2724649a-5bae-4b34-89c0-2e5ca6d3203b> ;
    skos:definition """A galvanometer is a type of ammeter: an instrument for detecting and measuring electric current. It is an analog electromechanical transducer that produces a rotary deflection of some type of pointer in response to electric current flowing through its coil in a magnetic field. The term has expanded to include uses of the same mechanism in recording, positioning, and servomechanism equipment.

[Summary provided by the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory.]


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: GALVANOMETER
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: In Situ/Laboratory Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Electrical Meters
