    skos:definition "Cryosphere Models are models that look at the Earth's cryosphere regions, specifically looking at frozen water, snow, permafrost, floating ice, and glaciers. The cryosphere component is directly related to ocean sea-level, therefore is indirectly related to changes in the atmosphere and biosphere."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "CRYOSPHERE MODELS"@en ;
