    skos:definition """Tree Rings, also known as annual rings or growth rings, are a sheath of
cells appearing as one of a series of concentric rings in the
cross-section of a woody stem.  Each ring is usually the result of a
single yearly growth flush starting in spring and ceasing in late summer."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "TREE RINGS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Allaby, M. 1998. A Dictionary of Ecology. Oxford University Press.  Oxford, New
York."""@en ] .

