<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/0f7493be-f2c7-427b-befb-d4e33f08016c> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3e8bc0c6-f599-4e23-9535-449af00edd61> ;
    skos:definition """Indian Remote Sensing (IRS) P2 was launched in 1994. This satellite carries one imaging sensor: Linear Imaging Self Scanner (LISS) 2. This satellite has a polar, circular, sun-synchronous 817-km orbit with a 24-day repeat cycle. Like the IRS-1A and -1B platforms, IRS-P2 has two identical LISS 2, but with a resolution of 32 m across-track and 37 m along-track. The total swath width on the IRS-P2 is 131 km.


