""",
        """2017-06-27 14:23:40.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Bowen Ratio Devices are instruments that measures the Bowen Ratio. Bowen ratio is used to describe the type of heat transfer in a water body. Heat transfer can either occur as sensible heat (differences in temperature without evapotranspiration) or latent heat (the energy required during a change of state, without a change in temperature). The Bowen ratio is the mathematical method generally used to calculate heat lost (or gained) in a substance; it is the ratio of energy fluxes from one state to another by sensible heat and latent heating respectively.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Bowen Ratio Devices are instruments that measures the Bowen Ratio. Bowen ratio is used to describe the type of heat transfer in a water body. Heat transfer can either occur as sensible heat (differences in temperature without evapotranspiration) or latent heat (the energy required during a change of state, without a change in temperature). The Bowen ratio is the mathematical method generally used to calculate heat lost (or gained) in a substance; it is the ratio of energy fluxes from one state to another by sensible heat and latent heating respectively."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bowen Ratio Devices"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Bowen Ratio Devices"@en ] .

