substance conducts electricity, as represented by the current density per
unit electrical- potential gradient in the direction of flow."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATMOSPHERIC CONDUCTIVITY"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 1998."@en ] .

