        """2022-08-10 09:28:09.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Esri ASCII raster format can be used to transfer information to or from other cell-based or raster systems. When an existing raster is output to an Esri ASCII-format raster, the file will begin with header information that defines the properties of the raster such as the cell size, the number of rows and columns, and the coordinates of the origin of the raster. The header information is followed by cell value information specified in space-delimited row-major order, with each row separated by a carriage return.
language code: en); 
""" ;
