Cambridge, Mass., NCC Blackwell; Blackwell Publishers.\r
From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.	<a
href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_Support_System">
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_Support_System</a>"""@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/20ee59ce-5b73-490f-a7f9-68436314a525> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/deac2632-5c17-4d15-ae92-c61ebc5a405a> ;
    skos:changeNote """2015-04-07 14:31:33.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (MMS SCM [20ee59ce-5b73-490f-a7f9-68436314a525,157873] - MAGNETOMETERS [deac2632-5c17-4d15-ae92-c61ebc5a405a,146671]); 
""",
        """2015-04-07 14:34:07.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
text: Search Coil Magnetometer
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Search Coil Magnetometer
provides direct measurements of
changes in the magnetic fields, using
something called an induction
magnetometer. The magnetometer
contains a coil of wire around a
ferromagnetic material. It is a basic law
of physics that a changing magnetic
field near such a coil will induce a
voltage. This voltage, in turn, can be
used to measure how the magnetic
field changes.
The SCM was developed at the
Laboratory for Plasma Physics in
Paris, France.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The Search Coil Magnetometer
provides direct measurements of
changes in the magnetic fields, using
something called an induction
magnetometer. The magnetometer
contains a coil of wire around a
ferromagnetic material. It is a basic law
of physics that a changing magnetic
field near such a coil will induce a
voltage. This voltage, in turn, can be
used to measure how the magnetic
field changes.
The SCM was developed at the
Laboratory for Plasma Physics in
Paris, France."""@en ;
