    skos:definition """Radiocarbon refers to radioactive carbon especially carbon-14, but also
carbon-10 and carbon-12. Carbon-14 is a heavy radioactive isotope of Carbon
having a mass of 14 and a half-life of 5730 +/-40 years. Carbon-14 is useful in
dating organic materials during the last 50,000 years."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "RADIOCARBON"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological
Institute."""@en ] .

