text: ERA 40 is a second generation reanalysis. It is the first reanalysis to directly assimilate satellite radiance data (TOVS, SSM/I, ERS and ATOVS). Cloud Motion Winds are also used. The result is better circulation over the tropics and southern hemisphere. However, unless comparing  to previous ERA-40 based results, it is recommended that the 3rd generation reanalyses, ERA-Interim or MERRA, be used for new research.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "ERA 40 is a second generation reanalysis. It is the first reanalysis to directly assimilate satellite radiance data (TOVS, SSM/I, ERS and ATOVS). Cloud Motion Winds are also used. The result is better circulation over the tropics and southern hemisphere. However, unless comparing  to previous ERA-40 based results, it is recommended that the 3rd generation reanalyses, ERA-Interim or MERRA, be used for new research."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/platforms> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ERA40DAS"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "ERA40 Data Assimilation System"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://climatedataguide.ucar.edu/climate-data/era40"@en ] .

