""",
        """2022-08-11 08:12:20.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: There are two main versions of the HDF library: HDF4 and HDF5. These two versions are not compatible and support for both will continue. However, the support for HDF4 will be limited to bug-fixes and building and testing on new platforms; no new features will be added. There are also two main versions of HDF-EOS that are based on the HDF libraries. HDF-EOS2.x versions are based on HDF4 and HDF-EOS5.x versions are based on HDF5. There are no HDF-EOS3 or HDF-EOS4 versions.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2022-08-11 08:12:50.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (There are two main versions of the HDF library: HDF4 and HDF5. These two versions are not compatible and support for both will continue. However, the support for HDF4 will be limited to bug-fixes and building and testing on new platforms; no new features will be added. There are also two main versions of HDF-EOS that are based on the HDF libraries. HDF-EOS2.x versions are based on HDF4 and HDF-EOS5.x versions are based on HDF5.); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "There are two main versions of the HDF library: HDF4 and HDF5. These two versions are not compatible and support for both will continue. However, the support for HDF4 will be limited to bug-fixes and building and testing on new platforms; no new features will be added. There are also two main versions of HDF-EOS that are based on the HDF libraries. HDF-EOS2.x versions are based on HDF4 and HDF-EOS5.x versions are based on HDF5."@en ;
