    skos:definition """WPM is a Chinese imager (developed at CAST) providing panchromatic imagery with 2 m resolution and multispectral RGB imagery of 8 m resolution. Scanning technique: Pushbroom, swath 60 km, possible to be pointed within a field of regard of ± 500 km. WPM has a mass of 263 kg, a power consumption of 80 W and a data rate of 240 Mbit/s. The WPM has focal plane adjustment and on-orbit calibration capabilities.

