        """2024-02-28 11:39:48.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A bin is a subset of genomic fragments that are believed to be from the same species in a metagenomic community. Contig binning aims to put the assembled genomic fragments, or contigs, from the same genome into the same bin. The contigs from these bins are then presented as a single collection to form metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs).
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "A bin is a subset of genomic fragments that are believed to be from the same species in a metagenomic community. Contig binning aims to put the assembled genomic fragments, or contigs, from the same genome into the same bin. The contigs from these bins are then presented as a single collection to form metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs)."@en ;
