text: 3-Wavelength Particle Soot Absorption Photometer Manufactured by Radiance Research
language code: en); 
""",
        """2024-12-19 15:30:29.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: An instrument that measures the absorption of light by particles (like soot) at three different wavelengths, allowing for a more detailed analysis of the particle composition and size distribution compared to a single-wavelength measurement. The method is based on the integrating plate technique in which the change in optical transmission of a filter caused by particle deposition on the filter is related to the light absorption coefficient of the deposited particles using Beers Law. Older versions operated at 1 wavelength (nominally 565 nm) while new versions have 3 wavelengths (467, 530 and 660 nm).
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "An instrument that measures the absorption of light by particles (like soot) at three different wavelengths, allowing for a more detailed analysis of the particle composition and size distribution compared to a single-wavelength measurement. The method is based on the integrating plate technique in which the change in optical transmission of a filter caused by particle deposition on the filter is related to the light absorption coefficient of the deposited particles using Beers Law. Older versions operated at 1 wavelength (nominally 565 nm) while new versions have 3 wavelengths (467, 530 and 660 nm)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PSAP"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "3-Wavelength Particle Soot Absorption Photometer Manufactured by Radiance Research"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://gml.noaa.gov/aero/instrumentation/psap.html"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/30a98319-e05b-4f35-9cdd-8f287f6c8300> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/0a184cdc-c074-4946-90a6-02f03c686341> ;
    skos:changeNote """2020-06-18 14:26:38.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (CMS-Flux-V1 [30a98319-e05b-4f35-9cdd-8f287f6c8300,560364] - Models/Analyses [113ecbc2-ab36-4d58-a96c-a6ce0106e749,541255]); 
""",
        """2020-06-18 14:36:55.0 [mmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Carbon Monitoring System Flux V1
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The CMS Methane (CH4) Flux for North America data set contains estimates of methane emission in North America based on an inversion of the GEOS-Chem chemical transport model constrained by Greenhouse Gases Observing SATellite (GOSAT) observations. The nested approach of the inversion enables large point sources to be resolved while aggregating regions with weak emissions and minimizing aggregation errors. The emission sources are separated into 12 different sectors as follows: Total, Oil/Gas, Coal, Cows, Waste (Landfills+ Wastewater), Biofuel, Rice, Other Anthropogenic, Biomass Burning, Wetlands, Soil Absorption, Other Natural. More details about the algorithm and error characterization can be found in Turner, Jacob, Wecht, et al. 2015.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2021-11-30 13:35:29.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (CMS-Flux-V1 [30a98319-e05b-4f35-9cdd-8f287f6c8300,826111] - Models [0a184cdc-c074-4946-90a6-02f03c686341,835911]); 
""",
        """2024-06-07 15:02:29.0 [tstevens]  
update AltLabel (Carbon Monitoring System Flux); 
update PrefLabel (CMS-Flux); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The CMS Methane (CH4) Flux for North America data set contains estimates of methane emission in North America based on an inversion of the GEOS-Chem chemical transport model constrained by Greenhouse Gases Observing SATellite (GOSAT) observations. The nested approach of the inversion enables large point sources to be resolved while aggregating regions with weak emissions and minimizing aggregation errors. The emission sources are separated into 12 different sectors as follows: Total, Oil/Gas, Coal, Cows, Waste (Landfills+ Wastewater), Biofuel, Rice, Other Anthropogenic, Biomass Burning, Wetlands, Soil Absorption, Other Natural. More details about the algorithm and error characterization can be found in Turner, Jacob, Wecht, et al. 2015."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/platforms> ;
    skos:prefLabel "CMS-Flux"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Carbon Monitoring System Flux"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://disc.gsfc.nasa.gov/datasets/CMS_CH4_FLX_NAD_1/summary?keywords=CMS_CH4_FLX_NAD"@en ] .

