text: A device used to identify the elemental composition of a material by detecting the characteristic X-rays emitted from a sample when bombarded with electrons, allowing for qualitative and quantitative analysis of the elements present in a specific area of a sample, typically attached to an electron microscope like a SEM (Scanning Electron Microscope) or TEM (Transmission Electron Microscope).
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "A device used to identify the elemental composition of a material by detecting the characteristic X-rays emitted from a sample when bombarded with electrons, allowing for qualitative and quantitative analysis of the elements present in a specific area of a sample, typically attached to an electron microscope like a SEM (Scanning Electron Microscope) or TEM (Transmission Electron Microscope)."@en ;
