        """2013-03-21 14:07:16.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A type of fog caused by the advection of moist air over a cold surface, and the consequent cooling of that air to below its dewpoint.

A very common advection fog is that caused by moist air over a cold body of water (sea fog).

Sometimes applied to steam fog.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """A type of fog caused by the advection of moist air over a cold surface, and the consequent cooling of that air to below its dewpoint.

A very common advection fog is that caused by moist air over a cold body of water (sea fog).

Sometimes applied to steam fog."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ADVECTION FOG"@en ;
