    skos:definition """Gas chromatography - specifically gas-liquid chromatography - involves a sample
being vapourised and injected onto the head of the chromatographic column. The
sample is transported through the column by the flow of inert, gaseous mobile
phase. The column itself contains a liquid stationary phase which is adsorbed
onto the surface of an inert solid."""@en ;
