        """2024-03-04 14:05:30.0 [tstevens]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Consolidated Prediction Format
language code: en); 
""",
        """2024-03-05 09:37:14.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The ILRS Predictions Formats Study Group created a Consolidated Prediction Format (CPF) for laser ranging that accurately predicts positions and ranges for a much wider variety of laser ranging targets than had been previously possible. The predictions provide daily tables of x,y, and z positions for each target that can be interpolated for very accurate predictions. There are three target classes consolidated under this format (1) Passive retro-reflectors (including earth orbiting, in lunar orbit, and on the moon) (2) asynchronous transponders, and (3) synchronous transponders. Aside from the expanded format capability, the new prediction system greatly improved tracking on low satellites because the full modeling potential of the orbit computation at the prediction center is passed on to the stations. Drag files and special maneuver files are no longer necessary.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The ILRS Predictions Formats Study Group created a Consolidated Prediction Format (CPF) for laser ranging that accurately predicts positions and ranges for a much wider variety of laser ranging targets than had been previously possible. The predictions provide daily tables of x,y, and z positions for each target that can be interpolated for very accurate predictions. There are three target classes consolidated under this format (1) Passive retro-reflectors (including earth orbiting, in lunar orbit, and on the moon) (2) asynchronous transponders, and (3) synchronous transponders. Aside from the expanded format capability, the new prediction system greatly improved tracking on low satellites because the full modeling potential of the orbit computation at the prediction center is passed on to the stations. Drag files and special maneuver files are no longer necessary."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/DataFormat> ;
    skos:prefLabel "CPF"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Consolidated Prediction Format"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://ilrs.gsfc.nasa.gov/data_and_products/formats/cpf.html"@en ] .

