        """2022-02-17 12:31:51.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (The Gulfstream Jet Prop Commander 1000 (AC-695A) is a stable high-wing, pressurized, twin-engine turboprop aircraft that is suitable for a variety of missions. Standard configuration allows for mission equipment, two pilots and one observer. However, the aircraft can be configured for two scientists/observers and mission equipment in the cabin.  NOAA’s AC-695A Jet Prop Commander is typically utilized by the National Weather Service (NWS) National Operational Hydrologic Remote Sensing Center (NOHRSC).); 
update Definition (NOAA); 
delete Resource (null); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Gulfstream Jet Prop Commander 1000 (AC-695A) is a stable high-wing, pressurized, twin-engine turboprop aircraft that is suitable for a variety of missions. Standard configuration allows for mission equipment, two pilots and one observer. However, the aircraft can be configured for two scientists/observers and mission equipment in the cabin.  NOAA’s AC-695A Jet Prop Commander is typically utilized by the National Weather Service (NWS) National Operational Hydrologic Remote Sensing Center (NOHRSC)."@en ;
