<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/376dde0f-a750-4138-91ce-8ca635bf05bd> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1a4e5774-7d4a-4ce7-9a4c-e2c72c8c377f> ;
    skos:changeNote """2022-08-02 17:02:40.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (SALT FLUX [376dde0f-a750-4138-91ce-8ca635bf05bd,1011360] - OCEAN SALINITY [1a4e5774-7d4a-4ce7-9a4c-e2c72c8c377f,1011299]); 
""",
        """2022-08-02 17:13:37.0 [sritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Sea salt aerosol, which originally comes from sea spray, is one of the most widely distributed natural aerosols. Sea salt aerosols are characterized as non-light-absorbing, highly hygroscopic, and having coarse particle size. Some sea salt dominated aerosols could have a single scattering albedo as large as ~0.97. Due to the hygroscopy, a sea salt particle can serve as a very efficient cloud condensation nuclei (CCN), altering cloud reflectivity, lifetime, and precipitation process. According to the IPCC report, the total sea salt flux from ocean to atmosphere is ~3300 Tg/yr
language code: en); 
""",
        """2022-08-11 11:55:47.0 [sritz]  
update Definition (https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/topics/atmosphere/aerosols/sea-salt, http://www-das.uwyo.edu/~geerts/cwx/notes/chap11/ocean_transport.html, https://science.nasa.gov/earth-science/oceanography/physical-ocean/salinity); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Sea salt aerosol, which originally comes from sea spray, is one of the most widely distributed natural aerosols. Sea salt aerosols are characterized as non-light-absorbing, highly hygroscopic, and having coarse particle size. Some sea salt dominated aerosols could have a single scattering albedo as large as ~0.97. Due to the hygroscopy, a sea salt particle can serve as a very efficient cloud condensation nuclei (CCN), altering cloud reflectivity, lifetime, and precipitation process. According to the IPCC report, the total sea salt flux from ocean to atmosphere is ~3300 Tg/yr"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "SALT FLUX"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/topics/atmosphere/aerosols/sea-salt, http://www-das.uwyo.edu/~geerts/cwx/notes/chap11/ocean_transport.html, https://science.nasa.gov/earth-science/oceanography/physical-ocean/salinity"@en ] .

