    skos:definition """[Source: eoportal.org,  http://directory.eoportal.org/presentations/6146/8664.html ]

IRS (Infrared System) of CAST, IRS is of IRMSS heritage. IRS is an imager with 4 spectral bands (0.76-0.90; 1.55-1.75; 2.08-2.35; 10.5-12.5 ) µm. The spatial resolution is halved with regard to IRMSS. 


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: IRS (CBERS)
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: Earth Remote Sensing Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Passive Remote Sensing
      Instrument_Type: Spectrometers/Radiometers
      Instrument_Subtype: Imaging Spectrometers/Radiometers
      Short_Name: IRS (CBERS)
      Long_Name: Infrared System (CBERS 3 and 4)
   End_Group
   Group: Associated_Platforms
      Short_Name: CBERS-4
      Short_Name: CBERS-3
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Near Infrared
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.76 μm -0.90 μm
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Infrared > Reflected
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 1.55 μm -1.75 μm
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Infrared > Reflected
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 2.08 μm -2.35 μm
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Infrared > Thermal
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 10.5 μm -12.5 μm
   End_Group
   Online_Resource: http://www.cbers.inpe.br/en/programas/cbers3-4.htm
   Online_Resource: http://directory.eoportal.org/presentations/6146/8664.html
   Creation_Date: 2008-09-10
   Group: Instrument_Logistics
      Instrument_Owner: Brazil National Institute for Space Research (INPE)
      Instrument_Owner: China National Space Administration
   End_Group
End_Group"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
