<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3f90fc9d-03a6-4297-a887-5295b2bd6ff9> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/6c5ca722-0bc7-4ccd-ad24-39b9d8710140> ;
    skos:changeNote """2025-01-22 08:46:38.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A polarimetric camera jointly designed and fabricated by the University of Arizona and the Jet Propulsion Laboratory. Developed for aerosol measurements from space, MSPI is well-suited for a variety of Stokes imaging applications from the UV through the Visible, NIR, and SWIR which demand polarimetric precision of better than 0.5% at time scales between DC and 25 Hz. The telescope is a three-mirror off-axis anastigmat, and images are built up through a push broom scan. Polarization modulation is provided by a novel implementation of dual photoelastic modulators set between quarter wave plates. The polarization is analyzed by an integrated assembly of rows of linear polarizers and dielectric filters applied directly above the focal plane array.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "A polarimetric camera jointly designed and fabricated by the University of Arizona and the Jet Propulsion Laboratory. Developed for aerosol measurements from space, MSPI is well-suited for a variety of Stokes imaging applications from the UV through the Visible, NIR, and SWIR which demand polarimetric precision of better than 0.5% at time scales between DC and 25 Hz. The telescope is a three-mirror off-axis anastigmat, and images are built up through a push broom scan. Polarization modulation is provided by a novel implementation of dual photoelastic modulators set between quarter wave plates. The polarization is analyzed by an integrated assembly of rows of linear polarizers and dielectric filters applied directly above the focal plane array."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "MSPI"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Multiangle SpectroPolarimetric Imager"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "David J. Diner, Ab Davis, Bruce Hancock, Sven Geier, Brian Rheingans, Veljko Jovanovic, Michael Bull, David M. Rider, Russell A. Chipman, Anna-Britt Mahler, and Stephen C. McClain, \"First results from a dual photoelastic-modulator-based polarimetric camera,\" Appl. Opt. 49, 2929-2946 (2010)."@en ] .

