    skos:definition """The goals of the sampling from the Pandalus are to determine the distribution and abundance of surface fishes, sample surface zooplankton, measure water temperature, salinity, and fluorescence in the water column, and collect zooplankton for later studies. Samples will be taken at specific station locations along the Seward hydrographic transect (GAK line).


