    skos:definition """Objective/Purpose:
The GEOS-3 Radar Altimeter is a precision satellite radar developed primarily to measure ocean surface topography and sea state. 

Summary of Parameters:
    Sea Surface Height
    Significant Wave Height
    Ocean Wind Speed


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: GEOS-3 ALTIMETER
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: Earth Remote Sensing Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Active Remote Sensing
      Instrument_Type: Altimeters
      Instrument_Subtype: Radar Altimeters
      Short_Name: GEOS-3 ALTIMETER
      Long_Name: GEOS-3 ALTIMETER
   End_Group
   Group: Associated_Platforms
      Short_Name: GEOS-3
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: RADIO
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 13.9 GHz
   End_Group
   Online_Resource: ftp://podaac.jpl.nasa.gov/allData/geos3/L2/docs/geos3_gdr.html#4.
   Sample_Image: http://podaac.jpl.nasa.gov/sites/default/files/content/Geos_NASA_Auto1.jpeg
   Creation_Date: 2013-05-16
   Group: Instrument_Logistics
      Instrument_Start_Date: 1975-04-14
      Instrument_Stop_Date: 1978-12-02
      Instrument_Owner: NASA
   End_Group
End_Group"""@en ;
