text: Advanced Coherent Radar Depth Sounder
language code: en); 
""",
        """2025-03-07 09:55:17.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Center for Remote Sensing of Ice Sheets (CReSIS) has developed radars (ACoRDS) that operate over the frequency range from 140 to 230 MHz with multiple receivers developed for airborne sounding and imaging of ice sheets. MCoRDS radars have an adjustable radar bandwidth of 20 MHz to 60 MHz. Multiple receivers permit digital beamsteering for suppressing cross-track surface clutter that can mask weak ice-bed echoes and strip-map synthetic aperture radar (SAR) images of the ice-bed interface. With 200 W of peak transmit power, a loop sensitivity > 190 dB is achieved. These radars are flown on twin engine and long-range aircraft including NASA P-3 and DC-8.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Center for Remote Sensing of Ice Sheets (CReSIS) has developed radars (ACoRDS) that operate over the frequency range from 140 to 230 MHz with multiple receivers developed for airborne sounding and imaging of ice sheets. MCoRDS radars have an adjustable radar bandwidth of 20 MHz to 60 MHz. Multiple receivers permit digital beamsteering for suppressing cross-track surface clutter that can mask weak ice-bed echoes and strip-map synthetic aperture radar (SAR) images of the ice-bed interface. With 200 W of peak transmit power, a loop sensitivity > 190 dB is achieved. These radars are flown on twin engine and long-range aircraft including NASA P-3 and DC-8."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ACORDS"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Advanced Coherent Radar Depth Sounder"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://airbornescience.nasa.gov/instrument/Multichannel_Coherent_Radar_Depth_Sounder"@en ] .

