    skos:definition """Ozone (O3) that is measured  in the lowest 10-20 km of the Atmosphere.
While the maximum concentration of ozone occurs between 20-25 km, a
high concentration of ozone close to the Earth's surface is considered a
public health threat."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
