    skos:definition """A DOBSON SPECTROPHOTOMETER is a photoelectric spectrophotometer
that is used to determine the ozone content of the atmosphere;
compares the solar energy at two wavelengths in the absorption
band of the ozone by permitting the radiation of each to fall
alternately upon a photocell."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "DOBSON SPECTROPHOTOMETERS"@en .

