<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/4698858b-bf39-4a2c-9713-e41757739eff> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/41adc080-c182-4753-9666-435f8b1c913f> ;
    skos:changeNote """2020-05-21 11:25:19.0 [tstevens] Rename Concept 
update PrefLabel (IMAGE PROCESSING); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Visualization / Image Processing services are defined as Data Analysis and Visualization Services that allow the user to view (Visualization) and/or manipulate (Image Processing) Earth Science data in a graphical (rather than numerical) format. These services may or may not include the ability for a user to view and/or manipulate data in a non-graphical (e.g., numerical) format, however, this ability would not be the primary method of operation of the service. EXAMPLES:
XV, GhostScript, ERDAS IMAGINE, Adobe PhotoShop."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "IMAGE PROCESSING"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "NASA GCMD"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/46a21779-809f-43db-b196-f98af4f21e03> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3d25724b-832f-4a61-b0b2-4f2ccecdba94> ;
    skos:changeNote """2021-05-11 09:42:28.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (MetOne BC 1050 Black Carbon Monitors [46a21779-809f-43db-b196-f98af4f21e03,606927] - Chemical Meters/Analyzers [3d25724b-832f-4a61-b0b2-4f2ccecdba94,598603]); 
""",
        """2021-05-11 09:44:37.0 [tstevens]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Met one Instruments, Inc. BC 1050 Series Black Carbon Monitors
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Met One Instruments, Inc. BC 1050 Series, Black Carbon Monitors, measures the absorption of particulate matter onto filter tape continuously. The BC 1050 monitor operates at 2-wavelengths and the BC 1054 operates at 10-wavelengths. The BC 1050 offers the user the ability to monitor absorption at near-IR (880 nm) and near-UV (375 nm) wavelengths simultaneously with a standard minimum time resolution of 1-minute. The BC 1054, multi-spectrum carbon monitor, measures the absorption at 375, 430, 470, 525, 565, 590, 660, 700, 880 and 950 nm with a standard time resolution of 1-minute. Optional 1-second time resolution is available for both the BC 1050 and the BC 1054.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Met One Instruments, Inc. BC 1050 Series, Black Carbon Monitors, measures the absorption of particulate matter onto filter tape continuously. The BC 1050 monitor operates at 2-wavelengths and the BC 1054 operates at 10-wavelengths. The BC 1050 offers the user the ability to monitor absorption at near-IR (880 nm) and near-UV (375 nm) wavelengths simultaneously with a standard minimum time resolution of 1-minute. The BC 1054, multi-spectrum carbon monitor, measures the absorption at 375, 430, 470, 525, 565, 590, 660, 700, 880 and 950 nm with a standard time resolution of 1-minute. Optional 1-second time resolution is available for both the BC 1050 and the BC 1054."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "MetOne BC 1050 Black Carbon Monitors"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Met one Instruments, Inc. BC 1050 Series Black Carbon Monitors"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.ecotech.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Met-One-Black-Carbon-Monitors-Datasheet.pdf"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/46a263bf-4448-421f-be9d-7628f3d03490> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1b41692e-c7fe-4567-bed9-b938a7400462> ;
    skos:changeNote """2021-08-05 17:20:37.0 [sritz]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: SONIC ANEMOMETER
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """A SONIC ANEMOMETER is an anemometer that measures linear
components of the wind vector by determining the effect of the
wind on transit times of acoustic pulses transmitted in opposite
directions across known paths; operates on the principle that
the propagation velocity of a sound wave in a moving medium is
equal to the velocity of sound with respect to the medium plus
the velocity of the medium; an absolute instrument with a very
short time constant and an absence of moving mechanical parts."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "SONIC ANEMOMETER"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "SONIC ANEMOMETER"@en ] .

