update PrefLabel (LAND SURFACE FEEDBACKS); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Land-surface processes through which climate system is controlled,
changed, or modulated. Land-surface feedbacks involve a perturbation
in a climate quantity that causes a change in a second quantity, and the
change in the second quantity ultimately leads to an additional change
in the first. Land-surface feedbacks often involve land-surface change or
change in terrestrial carbon stocks that in turn affect land-atmosphere
interaction."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "LAND SURFACE FEEDBACKS"@en ;
