<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/57854209-ce09-4dc9-90e2-5c4e1060fdad> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "AVIRIS-Next Generation"@en ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/944b7691-af37-4fb4-9393-c114e7997829> ;
    skos:changeNote """2018-02-22 16:59:36.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (AVIRIS-NG [57854209-ce09-4dc9-90e2-5c4e1060fdad,310587] - Imaging Spectrometers/Radiometers [944b7691-af37-4fb4-9393-c114e7997829,290619]); 
""",
        """2018-02-22 17:01:27.0 [sritz]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text:  Airborne Visible InfraRed Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation.
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Airborne Visible-Infrared Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation (AVIRIS-NG) has been developed to provide continued access to high signal-to-noise ratio imaging spectroscopy measurements in the solar reflected spectral range. AVIRIS-NG is expected to replace the AVIRIS-Classic instrument that has been flying since 1986.

AVIRIS-NG measures the wavelength range from 380 nm to 2510 nm with 5 nm sampling. Spectra are measured as images with 600 cross-track elements and spatial sampling from 0.3 m to 4.0 m from a Twin Otter platform. In the near future, a high altitude platform (NASA's ER-2) will be available. AVIRIS-NG has better than 95% cross-track spectral uniformity and >= 95% spectral IFOV uniformity.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2018-02-22 17:08:25.0 [sritz]  
update AltLabel ( Airborne Visible InfraRed Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation); 
""",
        """2021-10-15 08:49:23.0 [tstevens]  
update AltLabel (Airborne Visible-Infrared Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation); 
""",
        """2024-05-08 19:28:57.0 [mmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: null
text: AVIRIS-Next Generation
language code: en); 
update Definition (The Airborne Visible/Infrared Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation (AVIRIS-NG or AVIRIS-Next Generation) is the second of the NASA AVIRIS spectrometer Facility Instrument series. The AVIRIS-NG provides high signal-to-noise ratio imaging spectroscopy measurements in 425 contiguous spectral channels with wavelengths in the solar reflected spectral range (380-2510 nm) with 5 nm sampling. The AVIRIS-NG began operation in 2014. The AVIRIS-NG has flown on a variety of aircraft platforms including the Twin Otter, the King Air B-200, and NASA's high-altitude ER-2 aircraft. The AVIRIS-NG has better than 95% cross-track spectral uniformity and >= 95% spectral instantaneous field of view (IFOV) uniformity. Data from AVIRIS-NG have been applied to a wide range of studies in the fields of terrestrial and coastal aquatic plant physiology, atmospheric and aerosol studies, environmental science, snow hydrology, geology, volcanology, oceanography, soil and land management, agriculture, limnology, etc); 
update Definition (ORNL DAAC); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Airborne Visible/Infrared Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation (AVIRIS-NG or AVIRIS-Next Generation) is the second of the NASA AVIRIS spectrometer Facility Instrument series. The AVIRIS-NG provides high signal-to-noise ratio imaging spectroscopy measurements in 425 contiguous spectral channels with wavelengths in the solar reflected spectral range (380-2510 nm) with 5 nm sampling. The AVIRIS-NG began operation in 2014. The AVIRIS-NG has flown on a variety of aircraft platforms including the Twin Otter, the King Air B-200, and NASA's high-altitude ER-2 aircraft. The AVIRIS-NG has better than 95% cross-track spectral uniformity and >= 95% spectral instantaneous field of view (IFOV) uniformity. Data from AVIRIS-NG have been applied to a wide range of studies in the fields of terrestrial and coastal aquatic plant physiology, atmospheric and aerosol studies, environmental science, snow hydrology, geology, volcanology, oceanography, soil and land management, agriculture, limnology, etc"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "AVIRIS-NG"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Airborne Visible-Infrared Imaging Spectrometer - Next Generation"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "ORNL DAAC"@en ] .

