<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/59c3ceea-e637-4400-a980-5eaedfa4eb91> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/c39f54a3-efd0-4596-8d5b-fe7ab519d13f> ;
    skos:changeNote """2021-12-14 08:41:09.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (RR Neph [59c3ceea-e637-4400-a980-5eaedfa4eb91,835981] - NEPHELOMETERS [c39f54a3-efd0-4596-8d5b-fe7ab519d13f,828267]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "TSI Integrating Nephelometers are designed specifically for studies of direct radiative forcing of the Earth’s climate by aerosol particles, or studies of ground-based or airborne atmospheric visual air quality in clean areas. They may also be used as an analytical detector for aerosol particles whenever the parameter of interest is the light-scattering coefficient of the particles after a pretreatment step, such as heating, humidification, or segregation by size. The light-scattering coefficient is a highly variable aerosol property. Integrating Nephelometers measure the angular integral of light scattering that yields the quantity called the aerosol scattering coefficient, which is used in the Beer-Lambert Law to calculate total light extinction."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "RR Neph"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Radiance Research Nephelometer"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://airbornescience.nasa.gov/instrument/TSI_Neph"@en ] .

