    skos:definition """The Low-Energy Neutral Atom (LENA) Imager instrument on the IMAGE spacecraft
detects energetic neutral atoms (ENAs) with energies between 10 eV and 500 eV.
LENA's primary role is to image the outflow of low-energy ions from the polar
ionosphere. Thomas E. Moore, of the NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, is the
lead investigator for the LENA experiment.

For more information, see:
http://lena.gsfc.nasa.gov/"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
