    skos:changeNote """2021-12-01 12:44:46.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (HELIOS 2 [5d34bc0e-e9a2-422e-aa9d-8dcb826af251,826290] - Helios [b5e6d6de-2d7b-4876-86b1-cd94a494d44d,835930]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Helios 2 was launched into a solar orbit on 15 January 1976. It had a perihelion of 0.29 AU and an aphelion of 1 AU. Its orbit made it an ideal platform for making long baseline time-of-arrival measurements to obtain source direction. The satellite rotated with a ~ 1-s spin period. The mission ended in 1981.

Information provided by http://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/docs/heasarc/missions/helios2.html


