    skos:definition """Also called Pressure Altitude. Barometric Altitude is the altitude\r
which corresponds to a given value of atmospheric pressure according to\r
the ICAO standard atmosphere. It is the indicated altitude of a pressure\r
altimeter at an altimeter setting of 29.92 inches of mercury (1013.2\r
mb); therefore it is the indicated altitude above the 1013.2 mb\r
constant-pressure surface. RT"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "BAROMETRIC ALTITUDE"@en ;
