    skos:definition """A Snow Density Cutter is a metal device that cuts out exactly
100 cubic centimeters of snow. The metal device is then placed
on the balance and the snow's mass is recorded. The snow density
can be calculated by dividing the mass by its volume.

[Source: Teachers Experiencing Antarctica and the Arctic]"""@en ;
