        """2022-08-10 11:34:24.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Output format created by the GRIDFLOAT command (from ArcInfo Workstation) and by the Raster to Float tool in ArcGIS for Desktop. ESRI_GridFloat is an interchange format, used primarily for exchange with other programs. The semantics of ESRI_GridFloat are identical to those of ESRI_ASCII_Grid. In terms of format structure, however, there are two differences. First, in ESRI_GridFloat the gridded data values are in binary form, typically resulting in smaller files. Second, ESRI_GridFloat is a pair of files: a simple text file with extension .hdr that contains the same information as the first six lines of the equivalent ESRI_ASCII_Grid with one additional line; and the primary content of numeric values in binary form in a file with extension .flt.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Output format created by the GRIDFLOAT command (from ArcInfo Workstation) and by the Raster to Float tool in ArcGIS for Desktop. ESRI_GridFloat is an interchange format, used primarily for exchange with other programs. The semantics of ESRI_GridFloat are identical to those of ESRI_ASCII_Grid. In terms of format structure, however, there are two differences. First, in ESRI_GridFloat the gridded data values are in binary form, typically resulting in smaller files. Second, ESRI_GridFloat is a pair of files: a simple text file with extension .hdr that contains the same information as the first six lines of the equivalent ESRI_ASCII_Grid with one additional line; and the primary content of numeric values in binary form in a file with extension .flt."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/DataFormat> ;
    skos:prefLabel "GRIDFloat"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Esri GridFloat Output File"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000422.shtml"@en ] .

