    skos:definition """The Clouds and the Earth's Radiant Energy System Scanner (CERES)
is a broadband instrument that measures the TOA radiance in
three bands (0.3 to > 50 ?m (total), 0.3 - 5 ?m (shortwave),
8-12 ?m (longwave) at a spatial resolution of about 10 km at
nadir.

Additional information available at
"http://vortex.nsstc.uah.edu/~sundar/papers/conf/IGARSS2001.pdf"

[Summary provided by University of Alabama]"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "CERES SCANNER"@en ;
