""" ;
    skos:definition """Inclinometer:

1. An instrument used to determine the angle of the earth's
magnetic field in respect to the horizontal plane.

2. An instrument for showing the inclination of an aircraft or
ship relative to the horizontal.

[Source: The American Heritage Dictionary of the English Language:
Fourth Edition.  2000]"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "INCLINOMETERS"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "INCLINOMETERS"@en ] .

