update PrefLabel (COUPLED SYSTEM FEEDBACKS); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Processes or interactions between systems, such as the ocean and
atmosphere, through which the climate system is controlled, changed,
or modulated. Examples include process that influence the flux of heat,
freshwater, and radiatively active trace gases between the ocean and
atmosphere as well as those that influence the exchange of carbon
dioxide between the atmosphere and terrestrial biosphere."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "COUPLED SYSTEM FEEDBACKS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Adapted from the IPCC TAR (https://www.ipcc.ch/site/assets/uploads/2018/03/TAR-07.pdf) and the USGCRP Glossary (https://www.globalchange.gov/climate-change/glossary)"@en ] .

