    skos:changeNote """2019-10-04 16:29:34.0 [sritz]  
update Definition (The advanced Ozone Mapping and Profiler Suite (OMPS) tracks the health of the ozone layer and measures the concentration of 
ozone in the Earth's atmosphere.

OMPS consists of three spectrometers: a downward-looking nadir mapper, nadir profiler and limb profiler. The entire OMPS 
suite, OMPS-Nadir (OMPS-N) and OMPS-Limb (OMPS-L), currently fly on board the Suomi NPP spacecraft and are scheduled to fly 
on the JPSS-2 satellite mission.

OMPS-N will fly on the JPSS-1 satellite mission and will be used to generate total column ozone measurements.

Mass: 68 kilograms
Average Power: 108 Watts
Vendor: Ball Aerospace and Technologies Corp. (BATC), Boulder, CO
OMS Sensor Leads: Scott Janz (Goddard Space Flight Center), Glen Jaross (SSAI)
Purpose: To measure the global distribution of O3 (Ozone) in the stratosphere

More Information: https://www.jpss.noaa.gov/omps.html

