    skos:definition """The Advanced Microwave Scanning Radiometer-EOS (AMSR-E) is one of the Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency (JAXA) mission instruments flown on the Earth Observing System (EOS) Aqua spacecraft, which was launched May 4, 2002. A similar instrument (AMSR) was flown on the JAXA ADEOS-II spacecraft in December 2002.

AMSR-E monitors various atmospheric and surface water processes that influence weather and climate. It provides improved measurements of rain rates and greatly extends the spatial coverage of the Tropical Rainfall Measuring Mission (TRMM) satellite, while also measuring water vapor, sea surface winds, sea surface temperature, sea ice, soil moisture, snow cover, and the amount of water in clouds.

The AMSR-E is a 14-channel, 8-frequency passive microwave radiometer which measures microwave radiation from the Earth's surface and atmosphere. Frequencies of the AMSR-E are 6.9, 10.7, 18.7, 23.8, 36.5, and 89.0 (horizontal and vertical polarization), and 50.3 and 52.8 GHz (vertical polarization only). AMSR has a large antenna (2 meters, one of the largest), and a field of view of 7 km at 89 GHz and 60km at 6.9 GHz. It scans conically at an incidence angle of 55 degrees to achieve a 1600 km swath width. Data are externally calibrated by a cold sky temperature (2.7K) and a high-temperature hot load.

Key AMSR-E Facts
Heritage: SMMR (on Nimbus-7 and Seasat), SSM/I (on DMSP), AMSR (on ADEOS II)
Swath Width: 1445 km
Coverage: Global coverage every 1 to 2 days
Spatial Resolution: 6 km x 4 km (89.0 GHz), 14 km x 8 km (36.5 GHz), 32 km x 18 km (23.8 GHz), 27 km x 16 km (18.7 GHz), 51 km x 29 km (10.65 GHz), 74 km x 43 km (6.925 GHz)
Dimensions: Sensor Unit: 1.95 m x 1.7 m x 2.4 m (deployed); Control Unit: 0.8 m x 1.0 m x 0.6 m
Mass: 314 kg
Power: 350 W
Duty Cycle: 100%
View: Forward-looking conical scan
Incidence Angle: 55°
Instrument IFOV at Nadir: Ranges from 74 km x 43 km for 6.9 GHz to 6 km x 4 km for 89.0 GHz
Sampling Interval: 10 km for 6-36 GHz channels, 5 km for the 89 GHz channel
Accuracy: 1 K or better
Design Life: 3 years


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: AMSR-E
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: Earth Remote Sensing Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Passive Remote Sensing
      Instrument_Type: Spectrometers/Radiometers
      Instrument_Subtype: Imaging Spectrometers/Radiometers
      Short_Name: AMSR-E
      Long_Name: Advanced Microwave Scanning Radiometer-EOS
   End_Group
   Group: Associated_Platforms
      Short_Name: ADEOS-II
      Short_Name: AQUA
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Microwave
      Number_Channels: 12 Channels
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.34 - 4.35 cm / 6.9 - 89.0 GHz
   End_Group
   Online_Resource: http://wwwghcc.msfc.nasa.gov/AMSR/
   Online_Resource: http://aqua.nasa.gov/content/amsr-e
   Online_Resource: http://mirador.gsfc.nasa.gov/cgi-bin/mirador/collectionlist.pl?keyword=AMSR-E
   Online_Resource: http://sharaku.eorc.jaxa.jp/AMSR/index.html
   Sample_Image: http://wwwghcc.msfc.nasa.gov/AMSR/images/amsre_instrument.jpg
   Creation_Date: 2007-04-16
   Group: Instrument_Logistics
      Data_Rate: 87.4 kbps average, 125 kbps peak
      Instrument_Start_Date: 2002-06-18
      Instrument_Owner: JAPAN/JAXA
   End_Group
End_Group"""@en ;
