    skos:changeNote """2013-02-12 13:51:21.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ALTOCUMULUS UNDULATUS [73e102fa-3089-42c3-bd0f-4682f73fff0f,82161] - ALTOCUMULUS [01021105-60ed-479a-a35b-faa73e286264,82159]); 
""",
        """2013-03-20 16:40:57.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: (Also called billow cloud, windrow cloud, wave cloud.) A cloud variety composed of merged or separate elements that are elongated and parallel, either suggestive of ocean waves or arranged in ranks and files.

Sometimes two distinct wave systems are apparent (biundulatus). The formation is by gravity waves that exhibit broad, nearly parallel lines of cloud oriented normal to the wind direction, with cloud bases near an inversion surface.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """(Also called billow cloud, windrow cloud, wave cloud.) A cloud variety composed of merged or separate elements that are elongated and parallel, either suggestive of ocean waves or arranged in ranks and files.

Sometimes two distinct wave systems are apparent (biundulatus). The formation is by gravity waves that exhibit broad, nearly parallel lines of cloud oriented normal to the wind direction, with cloud bases near an inversion surface."""@en ;
