    skos:definition """The LISS-IV camera is a high resolution multi-spectral camera operating in three spectral bands (B2, B3, B4). LISS-IV can be operated in either of the two modes. In the multi-spectral mode (Mx), a swath of 23 Km (selectable out of 70 Km total swath) is covered in three bands, while in mono mode (Mono), the full swath of 70 Km can be covered in any one single band, which is selectable by ground command (nominal is B3 - Red band). The LISS-IV camera can be tilted up to +-26 degrees Celsius in the across track direction thereby providing a revisit period of 5 days.


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: LISS-IV
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: Earth Remote Sensing Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Passive Remote Sensing
      Instrument_Type: Spectrometers/Radiometers
      Instrument_Subtype: Imaging Spectrometers/Radiometers
      Short_Name: LISS-IV
      Long_Name: Linear Imaging Self Scanning Sensor iV
   End_Group
   Group: Instrument_Associated_Sensors
      Short_Name: CAMERAS
   End_Group
   Group: Associated_Platforms
      Short_Name: IRS-P6
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Visible
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.52 μm - 0.59 μm
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Visible
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.62 μm - 0.68 μm
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Near Infrared
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.76 μm - 0.86 μm
   End_Group
   Online_Resource: http://www.nrsa.gov.in/satellites/irs-p6.html
   Creation_Date: 2008-08-15
   Group: Instrument_Logistics
      Instrument_Start_Date: 2003-10-17
      Instrument_Owner: India
   End_Group
End_Group"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "LISS-IV"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Linear Imaging Self Scanning Sensor IV"@en ] .

