<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/79241b91-40b5-4a81-96c5-f92ab39584bd> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/944b7691-af37-4fb4-9393-c114e7997829> ;
    skos:definition """Ten years after the last spaceborne flights of the precursor
MOMS-01 in 1983/84, the new concept of a combined stereo and multi-
spectral payload, the Modular Optoelectronic Multispectral Stereo
Scanner (MOMS-02), was realized. It was successfully operated during
Space Shuttle flight STS-55 from April 26 to May 6, 1993, with an
average orbital altitude of 296 km and a geographic coverage of
+/- 28.5 latitude. MOMS-02 opens new horizons for Earth observation
from space using three-linear stereo cameras. Investigations of the
environment, agriculture, forestry and urban development as well as
digital mapping and landscape modelling with a high degree of
automation will be strongly improved by using the specific
capabilities of this sensor.

The entire MOMS-02 system was manufactured by DASA (German Aero-
space) under contract of Deutsche Agentur fuer Raumfahrt-Angelegen-
heiten (DARA) GmbH.
German Space Agency DARA GmbH.
Dept. for Special Applications
P.O.Box 300364
D-53183 Bonn
Federal Republic of Germany
Phone: +49-228-447-582
Fax:   +49-228-447-700
Technical Parameters:
---------------------
   The design features of the sensor provide at least the following
imagery characteristics:
i) three-linear stereo, ii) along track stereo, iii) high resolution,
iv) multispectral, v) combinations of stereo and multispectral.
The following spectral ranges and modes are provided:
Multispectral bands  spectral range  spatial resolution
band1                440-505 nm      13.5 m
band2                530-575 nm      13.5 m
band3                645-680 nm      13.5 m
band4                770-810 nm      13.5 m
Panchromatic bands  spectral range  spatial resolution
band5               520-760 nm      4.5 m
band6               520-760 nm      13.5 m
band7               520-760 nm      13.5 m
Mode  Channel Combination     No. of Data Takes
1  stereo channel 6,7; HR  15
2  multispectral channels 1,2,3,4 12
3  multispectral channels 3,4; stereo 6,7 7
4  multispectral channels 1,3,4; stereo 6 -
5  multispectral channels 1,3,4; stereo 7 1
6  multispectral channels 2,3,4; HR 13
7  multispectral channels 1,3,4; HR -
Mode 4 and 7 were not operated.
   MOMS02 is designed for spectral data acquisition in visible and near
infrared range (four channels) and for along-track stereo recording
using a panchromatic channel for one nadir and two off-nadir looking
modules. All stereo devices have equivalent bandpasses and provide a
ground pixel size of 4.5mx4.5m (nadir: band 5) and 13.5mx13.5m
(tilted optics: bands 6 and 7). A ground pixel size of 13.5mx13.5m
for the spectral channels is considered as a sound compromise between
a high spectral resolution and a reasonable signal to noise ratio.
   For all operated modes, except the full stereo mode, the nadir orien-
tation of the Space Shuttle was held within a limit of 1 degree. For
the stereo mode the roll angle limits had to be extended to 3 degrees
due to technical reasons.
Imaging Geometry:
-----------------
   The swath width for the high resolution channel can be as much as
37 km, depending on the recording mode, and 78 km for the other
channels. These values are relative to the nominal altitude of 296 km.
Because of the viewing angle of 21.4 degrees of the two off-nadir
stereo channels, the image swath on the Earth`s surface for these
channels is separated from the swath of the nadir channels by about
120 km. The three stereo cameras allow the imaging of a strip almost
simultaneously with three different viewing angles in a time distance
of about 20 seconds. Possible platform movements have to be compen-
sated.
Data Processing and Ordering:
-----------------------------

Additional information available at
"http://www.nz.dlr.de/moms2p/techdat/\""""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "MOMS-02"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Modular Optoelectronic Multispectral Stereo Scanner"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/792cf9f0-6d24-4de8-902c-b74e42c74fd3> a skos:Concept ;
