    skos:definition """Methane (CH4) is a colorless, odorless, flammable, greenhouse gas. It\r
is released naturally into the air from marshes, swamps, rice\r
fields, ruminant animals (such as cattle), and sewage sludge.  CH4 is\r
also released from methane-producing bacteria (methanogens) that live\r
in anaerobic places. [Solar Energy; v52n6; 467-477; 1994.] [Air, The\r
Nature of Atmosphere and the Climate; Michael Allaby; pages 39,40;\r
1992; Facts on File; New York] [Dictionary of Science;	R.K. Barnhart;\r
page 398; 1986; Houghton Mifflin Company; Boston.]"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "METHANE"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Atmospheric and Air Chemistry Glossary from the Sam Houston State University.\r
"http://www.shsu.edu/~chemistry/Glossary/glos.html\""""@en ] .

