        """2022-10-05 12:28:04.0 [tstevens]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Kipp and Zonen CNR4 Net Radiometer
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The CNR4 net radiometer measures the energy balance between incoming short-wave and long-wave Far Infrared (FIR) radiation versus surface-reﬂected short-wave and outgoing long-wave radiation. It consists of a pyranometer pair, one facing upward, the other facing downward, and a pyrgeometer pair in a similar conﬁguration. The pyranometer pair measures short-wave radiation and the pyrgeometer pair measures long-wave radiation.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The CNR4 net radiometer measures the energy balance between incoming short-wave and long-wave Far Infrared (FIR) radiation versus surface-reﬂected short-wave and outgoing long-wave radiation. It consists of a pyranometer pair, one facing upward, the other facing downward, and a pyrgeometer pair in a similar conﬁguration. The pyranometer pair measures short-wave radiation and the pyrgeometer pair measures long-wave radiation."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "CNR4"@en ;
