    skos:definition """The 3-axis fluxgate magnetometer onboard the AMPTE/IRM Satellite had a wide
dynamic range (0.1-60000 nT), a high resolution (16-bit analog to digital
conversion) and the capability to operate automatically or via telecommand in
two gain states. The sampling rate was 32 samples per second.
Reference:
Luehr, H., N. Kloecker, W. Oelschlaegel, B. Haeusler, and M. Acuna,
'The IRM fluxgate magnetometer', IEEE Trans., GE-23, 259, 1985.

Additional information available at
"http://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/database/MasterCatalog?sc=1984-088B\""""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "AMPTE/IRM MAGNETOMETER"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "AMPTE/IRM Three-axis Fluxgate Magnetometer"@en ] .

