    skos:definition """The advanced Ozone Mapping and Profiler Suite (OMPS) tracks the health of the ozone layer and measures the concentration of ozone in the Earth's atmosphere.

OMPS consists of three spectrometers: a downward-looking nadir mapper, nadir profiler and limb profiler. The entire OMPS suite, OMPS-Nadir (OMPS-N) and OMPS-Limb (OMPS-L), currently fly on board the Suomi NPP spacecraft and are scheduled to fly on the JPSS-2 satellite mission.

OMPS-N will fly on the JPSS-1 satellite mission and will be used to generate total column ozone measurements.

OMPS collects total column and vertical profile ozone data and continues the daily global data produced by current ozone monitoring systems—the Solar Backscatter Ultraviolet Radiometer (SBUV/2) and Total Ozone Mapping Spectrometer (TOMS)"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "OMPS-N"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Ozone Mapping and Profiler Suite - Nadir"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """http://www.jpss.noaa.gov/omps.html
https://jointmission.gsfc.nasa.gov/omps.html"""@en ] .

