    skos:definition """[Source: Earth Observation Satellites and Sensors for Risk Management, http://www.space-risks.com/SpaceData/index.php?Satellite_Name=SPOT+5&id_page=8 ] 

The panchromatic resolution is 2.5m / 5 m. Imagery at a resolution of 2.5 metres in the panchromatic band is obtained using a sampling concept unique to SPOT 5, called Supermode. This concept processes two 5-metre panchromatic images acquired simultaneously to generate a single image at a resolution of 2.5 metres.


