        """2024-03-05 12:44:12.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: It has become necessary, after more than 17 years of lunar laser ranging, to upgrade the data formats used to archive and disseminate the lunar laser ranging data type. This has been necessitated by current and
anticipated increases in precision of the observations, ultimately to the 1 mm level in the next few years. Other innovations in this format include record types for tracking system configuration changes and data
quality comments as well as a short normalpoint format for use in electronic data transfer.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """It has become necessary, after more than 17 years of lunar laser ranging, to upgrade the data formats used to archive and disseminate the lunar laser ranging data type. This has been necessitated by current and
anticipated increases in precision of the observations, ultimately to the 1 mm level in the next few years. Other innovations in this format include record types for tracking system configuration changes and data
quality comments as well as a short normalpoint format for use in electronic data transfer."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/DataFormat> ;
