    skos:definition """The Weather Research and Forecasting (WRF) Model is a next-generation mesocale\r
numerical weather prediction system designed to serve both operational\r
forecasting and atmospheric research needs. It features multiple dynamical\r
cores, a 3-dimensional variational (3DVAR) data assimilation system, and a\r
software architecture allowing for computational parallelism and system\r
extensibility. WRF is suitable for a broad spectrum of applications across\r
scales ranging from meters to thousands of kilometers."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "WEATHER RESEARCH/FORECAST MODELS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Weather Research and Forecasting (WRF) home page \r
http://www.wrf-model.org/"""@en ] .

