    skos:changeNote """2023-02-22 12:13:54.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (PRISMA [93f8f6c2-b613-4b7d-b400-af81291bbaf6,1232198] - Hyperspectral Spectrometers/Radiometers [d0341489-930a-4aa8-a3d3-ab851816058c,1224390]); 
""",
        """2023-02-22 12:15:50.0 [sritz]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: PRecursore IperSpettrale della Missione Applicativa
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: PRISMA carries two sensor instruments, the HYC (Hyperspectral Camera) module and the PAN (Panchromatic Camera) module. The HYC sensor is a prism spectrometer for two bands, VIS/NIR (Visible/Near Infrared) and NIR/SWIR (Near Infrared/Shortwave Infrared), with a total of 237 channels across both bands. Its primary mission objective is the high-resolution (30 m) hyperspectral imaging of land, vegetation, inner waters and coastal zones. The second sensor module, PAN, is a high-resolution (5 m) optical imager, and is co-registered with HYC data to allow testing of image fusion techniques.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "PRISMA carries two sensor instruments, the HYC (Hyperspectral Camera) module and the PAN (Panchromatic Camera) module. The HYC sensor is a prism spectrometer for two bands, VIS/NIR (Visible/Near Infrared) and NIR/SWIR (Near Infrared/Shortwave Infrared), with a total of 237 channels across both bands. Its primary mission objective is the high-resolution (30 m) hyperspectral imaging of land, vegetation, inner waters and coastal zones. The second sensor module, PAN, is a high-resolution (5 m) optical imager, and is co-registered with HYC data to allow testing of image fusion techniques."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PRISMA"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "PRecursore IperSpettrale della Missione Applicativa"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.eoportal.org/satellite-missions/prisma-hyperspectral"@en ] .

