""" ;
    skos:definition "The agricultural practice of producing or growing one single crop over a wide area. It is widely used in modern industrial agriculture  and its implementation has allowed for large harvests from minimal labor. However, monocultures can lead to the quicker spread of diseases, where a uniform crop is susceptible to a pathogen."@en ;
