<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/94358f5c-bb25-4c11-8131-466bec38e7ff> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/2ac83116-414b-44ce-a075-eb65f42e8232> ;
    skos:changeNote """2021-12-02 12:53:45.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ULH [94358f5c-bb25-4c11-8131-466bec38e7ff,835949] - Hygrometers [2ac83116-414b-44ce-a075-eb65f42e8232,827210]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """ULH measures water vapor at high accuracy in the upper troposphere and lower stratosphere to meet the following science objectives:

1. validation and scientific collaboration with NASA earth-monitoring satellite missions, principally the Aura satellite, http://aura.gsfc.nasa.gov/

2. observations of stratospheric trace gases in the upper troposphere and lower stratosphere from the mid-latitudes into the tropics,

3. sampling of polar stratospheric air and the break-up fragments of the air that move into the mid-latitudes, The ULH flights on Global Hawk will advance the state of the art technologically with remote command and control. ULH will provide real-time in-situ stratospheric water vapor measurements from Global Hawk. Additionally, ULH will make continuous measurements during long-duration flights up to 33 hours, which would be impossible with manned aircraft."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ULH"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Unmanned Aerial System Laser Hygrometer"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://espo.nasa.gov/instrument/ULH"@en ] .

