    skos:definition """The management and allocation of groundwater resources for
agricultural, industrial, and domestic use. Effective allocation requires
accurate knowledge about the spatial distribution of existing resources
and the relevant flow processes. Groundwater management techniques
include artificial recharge, aquifer storage and recovery, and water
saving irrigation techniques."""@en ;
