        """2020-01-29 17:08:37.0 [sritz]  
update Definition (The Ocean Surface Topography Mission (OSTM)/Jason-2 was a follow-on altimetric mission to the very successful TOPEX/Poseidon 
mission and Jason-1. It was a joint mission between NASA and CNES (French space agency). It launched 20 June 2008 and began 
data collection on 12 July 2008. OSTM measured significant wave height, sigma naught (sigma0), dry and wet troposphere and 
ionosphere, which can be used to calculate sea surface height and anomalies and total electron content.

https://podaac.jpl.nasa.gov/OSTM-JASON2

