<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/989e0558-a5fb-4758-bb82-c7d0a6a9f319> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/f2130ca3-3587-4312-b6d4-138456b5ea78> ;
    skos:changeNote """2018-03-07 08:46:26.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (NATIONAL SANITATION FOUNDATION WATER QUALITY INDEX [989e0558-a5fb-4758-bb82-c7d0a6a9f319,310707] - WATER QUALITY INDEXES [f2130ca3-3587-4312-b6d4-138456b5ea78,310635]); 
""",
        """2018-03-07 12:58:49.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A water quality index developed by the National Sanitation Foundation (NSF) in 1970 which provides a standardized method for comparing the water quality of various bodies of water. There are nine water quality parameters included in the index: dissolved oxygen (DO), fecal coliform, pH, biochemical oxygen demand (BOD) (5-day), temperature change (from 1 mile upstream), total phosphate, nitrate, turbidity, total solids.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "A water quality index developed by the National Sanitation Foundation (NSF) in 1970 which provides a standardized method for comparing the water quality of various bodies of water. There are nine water quality parameters included in the index: dissolved oxygen (DO), fecal coliform, pH, biochemical oxygen demand (BOD) (5-day), temperature change (from 1 mile upstream), total phosphate, nitrate, turbidity, total solids."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "NATIONAL SANITATION FOUNDATION WATER QUALITY INDEX"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "http://bcn.boulder.co.us/basin/watershed/wqi_nsf.html"@en ] .

