    skos:changeNote """2019-10-04 15:45:51.0 [sritz]  
update Definition (The Advanced Technology Microwave Sounder (ATMS) instrument is the next generation cross-track microwave sounder providing 
atmospheric temperature and moisture for operational weather and climate applications.

ATMS is a key instrument that collects microwave radiation from the Earth's atmosphere and surface all day and all night, 
even through clouds. ATMS currently flies on the Suomi NPP satellite mission and will fly on the JPSS-1 and JPSS-2 satellite 
missions.

More Information: https://www.jpss.noaa.gov/atms.html

Mass: approximately 75 kilograms
Average Power: 100 W
Development Institution: Northrop Grumman
ATMS Sensor Lead: Edward Kim, NASA GSFC
Purpose: To provide sounding profiles of atmospheric temperature and moisture


