    skos:changeNote """2024-04-05 09:08:45.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (EPIGENOME/EPIGENETICS [9b01ff92-8e7f-4852-9ad1-bb91d6528ffd,1633421] - OMICS [8eb84f36-f355-458b-889f-b37cfa120654,1633374]); 
""",
        """2024-04-05 09:09:21.0 [sritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Epigenetics (also sometimes called epigenomics) is a field of study focused on changes in DNA that do not involve alterations to the underlying sequence. The DNA nucleotides and the proteins that interact with DNA can have chemical modifications that change the degree to which genes are turned on and off. Certain epigenetic modifications may be passed on from parent cell to daughter cell during cell division or from one generation to the next. The collection of all epigenetic changes in a genome is called an epigenome.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Epigenetics (also sometimes called epigenomics) is a field of study focused on changes in DNA that do not involve alterations to the underlying sequence. The DNA nucleotides and the proteins that interact with DNA can have chemical modifications that change the degree to which genes are turned on and off. Certain epigenetic modifications may be passed on from parent cell to daughter cell during cell division or from one generation to the next. The collection of all epigenetic changes in a genome is called an epigenome."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "EPIGENOME/EPIGENETICS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Epigenetics"@en ] .

