language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """A SUNFLECK CEPTOMETER is an instrument that measures
instantaneous fluxes in solar radiation in the
photosynthetically active region (400-700 nm). Often used to
determine tree canopy transmittance of photosynthetically active
radiation."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
