    skos:definition """Hyper Spectral Imager (HySi-T) is one of the two onboard imaging payloads. It is an imager for ocean and atmosphere study of earth surface in large number of bands with high spectral resolution. The instrument shall have 64 bands in the spectral zone from 400 nm to 950nm. The imager using specific optics will collect and focus the solar reflection from the earth’s surface on to an area detector. The collecting optics for HySI-T is a multi-element lens assembly with a thermal filter at the front.


