    skos:definition "Drought duration refers to the length of time over which drought conditions persist. Drought frequency, duration, and severity are often used together as a means to describe and evaluate drought conditions in a given area (i.e., how often an area is affected by drought, how long is it affected, and how severely it is affected)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "DROUGHT DURATION"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Adapted from Brito, S. S., Cunha, A. P., Cunningham, C. C., Alvalá, R. C., Marengo, J. A. and Carvalho, M. A. (2018), Frequency, duration and severity of drought in the Semiarid Northeast Brazil region. Int. J. Climatol, 38: 517-529. doi:10.1002/joc.5225"@en ] .

