    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3d25724b-832f-4a61-b0b2-4f2ccecdba94> ;
    skos:changeNote """2021-08-05 11:54:10.0 [sritz]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: FLUORESCENCE SPECTROSCOPY
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Among instrumental techniques, fluorescence spectroscopy is
recognized as one of the more sensitive. In fluorescence, the
intensity of the emission of the sample is measured. The reason
for the high sensitivity of fluorescence techniques is that the
emission signal is measured above a low background level. This
is inherently more sensitive than comparing two relatively large
signals as in absorption spectroscopy. The sensitivity of
fluorescence techniques is as much as 1000 times more sensitive
than absorption spectroscopy.

Additional information available at
"http://www.pti-nj.com/tech_3.html\""""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "FLUORESCENCE SPECTROSCOPY"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "FLUORESCENCE SPECTROSCOPY"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a2987914-ed66-4b7c-964d-8eccf0174e57> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/08a4f002-f368-414d-b923-83dd498452d8> ;
    skos:changeNote """2012-06-26 15:51:21.0 [gee-cee] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ELECTRICAL PROPERTIES [a2987914-ed66-4b7c-964d-8eccf0174e57,40133] - ICE CORE RECORDS [08a4f002-f368-414d-b923-83dd498452d8,40095]); 
""",
        """2012-07-23 15:30:29.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: An important baseline measurement in ice cores is electrical conductivity. Electrical conductivity measurements (ECM) of the core is a very rapid method to indicate how acidic the core is without the chemical detail of the ion analyses. The value of the measurement is that it can be done for the whole length of the core in high resolution and provide an immediate picture of the core and allow quick detection of interesting areas, such as a volcanic eruptions. Because it is a high resolution, continuous measurement it can be used, along with the other measurements, for time frequency analysis in order to identify cycles in the climate signal.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "An important baseline measurement in ice cores is electrical conductivity. Electrical conductivity measurements (ECM) of the core is a very rapid method to indicate how acidic the core is without the chemical detail of the ion analyses. The value of the measurement is that it can be done for the whole length of the core in high resolution and provide an immediate picture of the core and allow quick detection of interesting areas, such as a volcanic eruptions. Because it is a high resolution, continuous measurement it can be used, along with the other measurements, for time frequency analysis in order to identify cycles in the climate signal."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ELECTRICAL PROPERTIES"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "GISP2 (Greenland) Ice Cores and Climate Change: http://www.gisp2.sr.unh.edu/GISP2/MoreInfo/Ice_Cores_Past.html"@en ] .

