""",
        """2012-06-26 11:44:45.0 [gee-cee] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (PALMER DROUGHT SEVERITY INDEX [a43850a1-7b00-4993-80ff-753c2b5c4015,20045] - DROUGHT INDICES [f50672b3-13d8-4206-b6c9-a1f9891ea470,39837]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The Palmer Index or the Palmer Drought Severity Index (PDSI) is an index\r
formulated by Palmer (1965) and compares the actual amount of precipitation\r
received in an area during a specified period with the normal or average amount
expected during that same period.\r
<P>\r
The PDSI is based on a procedure of hydrologic or water balance accounting by\r
which excesses or deficiences in moisture are determined in relation to average
climatic values."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PALMER DROUGHT SEVERITY INDEX"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Palmer, W.C., 1965: <i>Meteorological Drought Research Paper 45</i>, U.S.\r
Weather Bureau, Washington, D.C.\r
From: American Meterological Society, 2000: The Glossary of Meteorology, 2nd\r
edition, Boston, MA\r
See also "http://www.drought.noaa.gov/palmer.html\""""@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a4390c3d-cffa-43ee-8e91-49c6d49ac371> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/2e83362e-d8f8-4bca-83fd-bae360ebe94b> ;
    skos:definition """Radiation with wavelengths roughly between 200 and 400 nanometers.
These wavelengths are shorter than those which characterize visible
light. Observations from satellites in the UV and extreme UV (EUV)
wavelengths have demonstrated the sun's UV variability over short time
scales of days and weeks. UV variability is linked to solar magnetic
activity phenomena such as flares and plages. Studies of the UV and EUV
irradiance variability may have indicated influences on the Earth's
climate dynamics."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "SOLAR ULTRAVIOLET EMISSIONS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Foukal, P., ed. 1987. Solar Radiative Output Variation: Proceedings of a
Workshop held Nov. 9-11, 1987 at NCAR, Boulder, CO. Cambridge Research and
Instrumentation, Inc."""@en ] .

