    skos:definition """Measurements related to the signal recorded by the sensor.\r
<I>Phase</I>: A property of a periodic phenomenon, for example a\r
wave, referring to its starting point or advancement (fraction) relative\r
to an arbitrary origin.  For example, the angle of a complex number (ie.,\r
the waves are out-of-phase).	<I>Amplitude</I>: Measure of the strength\r
of a signal, and in particular the strength or "height" of an\r
electromagnetic wave (units of voltage)."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
