""",
        """2022-08-16 13:41:53.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The National Indicator Data Set (NIDS) is a minimum group of indicators introduced by the National Department of Health that every public health facility is expected to collect, use and report on. Facilities are required to report only on indicators in which they render the service according to their service package. The NIDS is use for monitoring and tracking progress with the implementation of national strategic goals, objectives and priority health programmes. The NIDS will help the Department of Health to identify the needs in the healthcare system and provide managers with information to guide programme development and budgeting, provide support to improve the healthcare system, and demonstrate national commitment to globally accepted measures of care.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2022-08-16 13:42:06.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The National Indicator Data Set (NIDS) is a minimum group of indicators introduced by the National Department of Health that every public health facility is expected to collect, use and report on. Facilities are required to report only on indicators in which they render the service according to their service package. The NIDS is use for monitoring and tracking progress with the implementation of national strategic goals, objectives and priority health programmes. The NIDS will help the Department of Health to identify the needs in the healthcare system and provide managers with information to guide programme development and budgeting, provide support to improve the healthcare system, and demonstrate national commitment to globally accepted measures of care."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/DataFormat> ;
    skos:prefLabel "NIDS"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "National Indicator Data Set"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a83052ef-9b98-4cb3-9bed-b0c9059812e5> a skos:Concept ;
