        """2018-03-06 15:29:26.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (Naturally present as a result of animal respiration, the decay of organic matter, and the decomposition of certain minerals. It is the major source of acidity in unpolluted water samples. Surface waters typically contain less than 10 ppm (mg/L) dissolved CO2, while ground waters, particularly if deep, may contain several hundred ppm (mg/L).); 
update Definition (Houghton, J. 1997. Global Warming: The Complete Briefing, 2nd. ed. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, UK. Maunder, W.J. 1994. Dictionary of Global Climate Change, 2nd ed. Chapman and Hall, NY. ); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Naturally present as a result of animal respiration, the decay of organic matter, and the decomposition of certain minerals. It is the major source of acidity in unpolluted water samples. Surface waters typically contain less than 10 ppm (mg/L) dissolved CO2, while ground waters, particularly if deep, may contain several hundred ppm (mg/L)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "DISSOLVED CARBON DIOXIDE"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Houghton, J. 1997. Global Warming: The Complete Briefing, 2nd. ed. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, UK. Maunder, W.J. 1994. Dictionary of Global Climate Change, 2nd ed. Chapman and Hall, NY."@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a9bd961e-1063-4f37-99b6-ecd77aa9eb40> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/4190ebdc-e89a-4f3f-bc74-b2af4c68d009> ;
    skos:definition """The AIRS (Atmospheric Infrared Sounder) instrument is a high spectral resolution grating spectrometer containing 2378 infrared channels in the 3.74 to 15.4 micron spectral range for obtaining atmospheric temperature profiles and a variety of additional Earth/atmosphere products.  AIRS is centered on measuring accurate temperature and humidity profiles throughout the atmosphere.  AIRS also provides four visible/near-infrared channels (0.4 - 1.0 &#956;m) to characterize cloud and surface properties.

Key AIRS Facts
Heritage: Advanced Moisture and Temperature Sounder (AMTS), High
Resolution Infrared Radiation Sounder (HIRS)
Instrument Type: Temperature controlled (155 K) array grating spectrometer, plus a visible/near-infrared photometer
Aperture: 10 cm
Swath Width: 1650 km
Coverage: Global coverage every 1 to 2 days
Spatial Resolution: Infrared: 13.5 km at nadir; Visible/near-infrared: 2.3 km at nadir
Dimensions: 116.5 cm x 80 cm x 95.3 cm
Mass: 177 kg
Power: 180/220 W (beginning/end of life)
Duty Cycle: 100%
Field of View (FOV): ± 49.5° cross-track from nadir
Instrument IFOV (track/scan): Infrared: 1.1° x 0.6° (13.5 km x 7.4 km at nadir); Visible/near-infrared: 0.149° x 0.190° (1.8 km x 2.3 km at nadir)
Scan Period: 2.667 s
Scan Sampling (scan/track): Infrared: 90 x 1 (1.1° spacing), in 2 s; visible/near-infrared: 720 x 9 (0.138° x 0.185° spacing), in 2 s
Design Life: 5 years


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: AIRS
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: Earth Remote Sensing Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Passive Remote Sensing
      Instrument_Type: Profilers/Sounders
      Short_Name: AIRS
      Long_Name: Atmospheric Infrared Sounder
   End_Group
   Group: Associated_Platforms
      Short_Name: AQUA
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Visible
      Number_Channels: 2 Channels
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.4 μm - 0.68 μm
      Spectral_Frequency_Resolution: &#955;/&#916;&#955; 1200 nominal
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Near Infrared
      Number_Channels: 2 Channels
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 0.71 μm - 0.94 μm
      Spectral_Frequency_Resolution: &#955;/&#916;&#955; 1200 nominal
   End_Group
   Group: Spectral_Frequency_Information
      Wavelength_Keyword: Infrared > Thermal
      Number_Channels: 2378
      Spectral_Frequency_Coverage_Range: 3.74 μm - 15.4 μm
      Spectral_Frequency_Resolution: &#955;/&#916;&#955; 1200 nominal
   End_Group
   Online_Resource: http://airs.jpl.nasa.gov/
   Online_Resource: http://aqua.nasa.gov/content/airs
   Online_Resource: http://disc.gsfc.nasa.gov/AIRS/index.shtml
   Online_Resource: http://mirador.gsfc.nasa.gov/cgi-bin/mirador/presentNavigation.pl?tree=project&project=AIRS
   Sample_Image: http://airs.jpl.nasa.gov/system/content_pages/main_images/13_13_8262767875_dff40d0f0b_z.jpg
   Creation_Date: 2007-04-16
   Group: Instrument_Logistics
      Data_Rate: 1.27 Mbps
      Instrument_Start_Date: 2002-08-31
      Instrument_Owner: USA/NASA
   End_Group
End_Group"""@en ;
