<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/aad49974-99ab-4623-a716-ea73e2f46ad1> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/55715ed3-471e-46a8-97b6-b463708a2cbe> ;
    skos:changeNote """2021-10-20 09:26:16.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (POTENTIAL VORTICITY [aad49974-99ab-4623-a716-ea73e2f46ad1,778213] - VORTICITY [55715ed3-471e-46a8-97b6-b463708a2cbe,776114]); 
""",
        """2021-10-21 15:52:07.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The quantity which is proportional to the dot product of vorticity and stratification. This quantity, following a parcel of air or water, can only be changed by diabatic or frictional processes. It is a useful concept for understanding the generation of vorticity in cyclogenesis (the birth and development of a cyclone), especially along the polar front, and in analyzing flow in the ocean.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The quantity which is proportional to the dot product of vorticity and stratification. This quantity, following a parcel of air or water, can only be changed by diabatic or frictional processes. It is a useful concept for understanding the generation of vorticity in cyclogenesis (the birth and development of a cyclone), especially along the polar front, and in analyzing flow in the ocean."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
