    skos:definition """RAWINSONDES are an upper-air sounding that includes
determination of wind speeds and directions. In the past, data
was collected by tracking a balloon-borne radiosonde with a
radio direction finder.  Nowadays, GPS or Loran radio navigation
signals measure position or radiosonde velocity."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "RAWINSONDES"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
