    skos:definition "Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Sirenia are large, fusiform, slow moving herbivorous aquatic mammals with broad backs tapering to paddle-like, dorso-ventrally flattened tails. Their heavy bones act as ballasts to counteract their blubber buoyancy. Dugongs are more streamlined than manatees, lack nails on their flippers and have a bi-lobe tai."@en ;
