    skos:definition """HUMIDITY SENSORS are devices that receive a signal or stimulus
(as heat or pressure or light or motion etc.) and responds to
it, in this case humidity or some measure of the water vapor
content of air.


Group: Instrument_Details
   Entry_ID: HUMIDITY SENSORS
   Group: Instrument_Identification
      Instrument_Category: In Situ/Laboratory Instruments
      Instrument_Class: Temperature/Humidity Sensors
      Short_Name: HUMIDITY SENSORS
   End_Group
   Group: Associated_Platforms
      Short_Name: SGO
   End_Group
   Creation_Date: 2007-07-10
End_Group"""@en ;
