        """2021-04-29 12:47:20.0 [mmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: COSMO-SkyMed Second Generation (CSG)
language code: en); 
update PrefLabel (COSMO-SkyMed Second Generation (CSG)); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: Italy's second generation COSMO-SkyMed constellation of two satellites (CSG-1 and CSG-2), also referred to as CSG (COSMO-SkyMed Seconda Generazione), aims at improving the quality of the imaging service, providing the end users with enhanced capabilities in terms of higher number of images and image quality (larger swath and finer spatial and radiometric resolution) with respect to the current COSMO-SkyMed constellation, referred to as CSK.

See also
https://earth.esa.int/web/guest/content/-/article/cosmo-skymed-second-generation-ready-for-take-off
https://directory.eoportal.org/web/eoportal/satellite-missions/c-missions/cosmo-skymed-second-generation
language code: en); 
""",
