    skos:definition "PALACE FLOATS measure profiles of ocean salinity and temperature. Measurements are made as the floats ascend to a drifting horizon. They do this by changing their buoyancy internally.  Periodically, the floats rise to the surface, where the data is transmitted via satellite."@en ;
