    skos:changeNote """2024-01-17 15:08:14.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (obs_seq [b4daf648-f134-42c4-8840-b0966e233554,1558636] - Data Format [8e770fe1-6e82-43aa-9f8a-75d217d7e6cb,1554670]); 
""",
        """2024-01-17 15:10:37.0 [tstevens]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Observation sequence file format
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The observation sequence file format is a linked list format that is widely used in the Earth Science data assimilation community. It differs from other other file formats such as netCDF and HDF in that it allows for the specification of the observational error variance for a given observation, a necessary quantity for ensemble data assimilation applications. The file format also provides for a mapping of specific Earth Science observations to generic physical quantities such as temperature, salinity, electron density, zonal velocity, etc. 

The obs_seq file format has been used in hundreds of scientific publications, by users of the Data Assimilation Research Testbed (DART). DART is a widely used data assimilation system that interfaces with models that span the Earth System: meteorological, space weather, oceanographic, hydrological, etc.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The observation sequence file format is a linked list format that is widely used in the Earth Science data assimilation community. It differs from other other file formats such as netCDF and HDF in that it allows for the specification of the observational error variance for a given observation, a necessary quantity for ensemble data assimilation applications. The file format also provides for a mapping of specific Earth Science observations to generic physical quantities such as temperature, salinity, electron density, zonal velocity, etc. 

The obs_seq file format has been used in hundreds of scientific publications, by users of the Data Assimilation Research Testbed (DART). DART is a widely used data assimilation system that interfaces with models that span the Earth System: meteorological, space weather, oceanographic, hydrological, etc."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/DataFormat> ;
    skos:prefLabel "obs_seq"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Observation sequence file format"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://docs.dart.ucar.edu/en/latest/guide/detailed-structure-obs-seq.html"@en ] .

