        """2024-03-05 12:38:37.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The IGS SSR binary format uses the basic structure of RTCM3 developed by the RTCM SC-104. RTCM proprietary message types are assigned to specific companies and organizations in the RTCM 10403.3 Standard for the broadcast of proprietary information. The format of the proprietary messages corresponds to the RTCM messages, in that the transport layer is defined in the same way, and the first data field is a 12-bit message number for an organization. The organization is free to define several sub-types of messages, but they must all utilize the assigned message type.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The IGS SSR binary format uses the basic structure of RTCM3 developed by the RTCM SC-104. RTCM proprietary message types are assigned to specific companies and organizations in the RTCM 10403.3 Standard for the broadcast of proprietary information. The format of the proprietary messages corresponds to the RTCM messages, in that the transport layer is defined in the same way, and the first data field is a 12-bit message number for an organization. The organization is free to define several sub-types of messages, but they must all utilize the assigned message type."@en ;
