    skos:definition """SIDE-SCAN SONAR is a method of surveying the bottom of the ocean
or other body of water to obtain detailed acoustic images,
frequently used to locate debris likely form aircraft accidents
or shipwrecks; the acoustic beam is directed perpendicularly to
the direction of travel."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
