    skos:definition """A VISIBLE SPECTROMETER is a spectroscope used similarly like the
UV spectroscope, which is used for obtaining a mass spectrum of
visible light in the electromagnetic spectrum by deflecting the
visible light ions into a thin slit and then measuring the ion
current with an electrometer."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "VISIBLE SPECTROMETER"@en .

