        """2024-02-28 12:17:14.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: DNA metabarcoding is a developing approach that identifies multiple species from a mixed sample (bulk DNA or eDNA) based on high-throughput sequencing (HTS) of a specific DNA marker. It differs from conventional DNA barcoding (usually based on Sanger sequencing of individual specimens) because the amount of DNA sequence data derived by HTS allows taxonomy to be rapidly assigned to many species present in a sample.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "DNA metabarcoding is a developing approach that identifies multiple species from a mixed sample (bulk DNA or eDNA) based on high-throughput sequencing (HTS) of a specific DNA marker. It differs from conventional DNA barcoding (usually based on Sanger sequencing of individual specimens) because the amount of DNA sequence data derived by HTS allows taxonomy to be rapidly assigned to many species present in a sample."@en ;
