""" ;
    skos:definition """The Lake Renegade Seawolf (LA-27) is a rugged, adaptable, single turbo-charged piston engine amphibious aircraft designed for nearshore low-level surveys. The aircraft is equipped with external fuel tanks, bubble windows, and NATO hardpoints. A standard crew consists of one pilot and up to three scientists. The Lake aircraft has been used for biological surveys including red drum, sea turtle and marine mammal surveys, as well as on site terrain observations. 

[Photo and text provided by NOAA, 
http://www.aoc.noaa.gov/aircraft_lake.htm ]


