text: The quantification of the precise amount of a specific DNA or RNA molecule in a sample. Absolute abundance provides the quantitative abundance of DNA or RNA in a sample, as opposed to the relative abundance produced by traditional PCR methods. Two common methods to determine absolute abundance include:
