Molecular methods used in qPCR
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The quantification of the precise amount of a specific DNA or RNA molecule in a sample. Absolute abundance provides the quantitative abundance of DNA or RNA in a sample, as opposed to the relative abundance produced by traditional PCR methods. Two common methods to determine absolute abundance include:
Cell-based methods such as flow cytometry used in ddPCR
Molecular methods used in qPCR"""@en ;
