insert Definition (id: null
text: Harmony is a constellation of two SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) equipped satellites operated by the European Space Agency (ESA) as an Earth Explorer mission, which will run in tandem with a Sentinel-1 satellite. Until their design life of five years comes to an end, they will monitor changes in the Earth’s surface, as well as monitor ocean surface conditions such as wind, currents, and temperature.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Harmony is a constellation of two SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) equipped satellites operated by the European Space Agency (ESA) as an Earth Explorer mission, which will run in tandem with a Sentinel-1 satellite. Until their design life of five years comes to an end, they will monitor changes in the Earth’s surface, as well as monitor ocean surface conditions such as wind, currents, and temperature."@en ;
