    skos:prefLabel "EROS-B1"@en .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/cea7a056-9bc7-43be-a689-8a15fac587b7> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/8e8b7689-0a8e-47a4-9c68-5f6a207104d5> ;
    skos:definition """The YOHKOH satellite, also called "Sunbeam" was launched into
space from the Kagoshima Space Center (KSC) in Southern
Japan. This is a project of the Japanese Institute of Space and
Astronautical Science (ISAS). The scientific objective has been
to observe the energetic phenomena taking place on the Sun,
specifically solar flares in x-ray and gamma-ray emissions.

Instruments on the satellite:

the Bragg Crystal Spectrometer (BCS)
the Wide Band Spectrometer (WBS)
the Soft X-Ray Telescope (SXT)
the Hard X-Ray Telescope (HXT)

Additional information available at
"http://hesperia.gsfc.nasa.gov/sftheory/yohkoh.htm"

[Summary provided by NASA]


