<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d2e93932-0231-4b23-af2f-217c6315a95e> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3487d350-a5a5-43d9-a60d-c1407dd2f0ce> ;
    skos:changeNote """2013-02-14 14:11:20.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ABSORPTION [d2e93932-0231-4b23-af2f-217c6315a95e,82301] - CLOUD RADIATIVE TRANSFER [3487d350-a5a5-43d9-a60d-c1407dd2f0ce,82135]); 
""",
        """2013-03-21 14:46:27.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The process in which incident radiant energy is retained by a substance.

A further process always results from absorption, that is, the irreversible conversion of the absorbed radiation into some other form of energy within and according to the nature of the absorbing medium. The absorbing medium itself may emit radiation, but only after an energy conversion has occurred.
See attenuation.

The taking up or assimilation of one substance by another.

The substances may combine chemically, or the absorption may just correspond to a physical solubility.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The process in which incident radiant energy is retained by a substance.

A further process always results from absorption, that is, the irreversible conversion of the absorbed radiation into some other form of energy within and according to the nature of the absorbing medium. The absorbing medium itself may emit radiation, but only after an energy conversion has occurred.
See attenuation.

The taking up or assimilation of one substance by another.

The substances may combine chemically, or the absorption may just correspond to a physical solubility."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ABSORPTION"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "American Meteorological Society (http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Main_Page)"@en ] .

