""",
        """2024-09-23 14:49:20.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A new index that is called as the temperature concentration index (TCI) was developed in the present study to investigate the concentration of temperature in Iran based on the two known inspiring patterns of Gibbs–Martin (Am Sociol Rev 27:667–677, 1962) and Oliver (Prof Geogr 32:300–309, 1980). The developed index was classified based on three methods, including the Oliver’ classification (1980), the coefficient of variation of temperature data, and coefficient of variation of TCI values. The results show that all the three classification methods represent almost similar classes for the TCI.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "A new index that is called as the temperature concentration index (TCI) was developed in the present study to investigate the concentration of temperature in Iran based on the two known inspiring patterns of Gibbs–Martin (Am Sociol Rev 27:667–677, 1962) and Oliver (Prof Geogr 32:300–309, 1980). The developed index was classified based on three methods, including the Oliver’ classification (1980), the coefficient of variation of temperature data, and coefficient of variation of TCI values. The results show that all the three classification methods represent almost similar classes for the TCI."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "TEMPERATURE CONCENTRATION INDEX (TCI)"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13762-018-1739-2"@en ] .

