    skos:changeNote """2024-06-03 16:30:54.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ALTIUS [dbf8a3ac-de82-4c55-aa24-e820f0370747,1708977] - Hyperspectral Spectrometers/Radiometers [d0341489-930a-4aa8-a3d3-ab851816058c,1700929]); 
""",
        """2024-06-03 16:33:55.0 [mmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Atmospheric Limb Tracker for the Investigation of the Upcoming Stratosphere
language code: en); 
insert Definition (id: null
text: The ALTIUS instrument is a three-channel hyperspectral imaging spectrometer that conducts a spectroscopic survey of the Earth’s atmosphere in the ultraviolet (UV), visible (VIS) and near infrared (NIR) spectral ranges.  The ALTIUS instrument observes the ozone from side-on, at Earth’s limb, with a 1 km vertical resolution. This limb-sounding technique allows ozone to be viewed at different altitudes, thereby providing vertical profiles of different ozone concentrations, providing a 2D image of ozone in the atmosphere. In addition to nominal limb observations, the instrument will also perform solar and stellar occultation observations in the dark limb.  The channels that the instruments images in are provided:

Ultraviolet channel (UV) - 0.25 µm - 0.355 µm 

Visible channel (VIS) - 0.44 µm - 0.675 µm

Near Infrared Channel (NIR) - 0.6 µm - 1.02 µm
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The ALTIUS instrument is a three-channel hyperspectral imaging spectrometer that conducts a spectroscopic survey of the Earth’s atmosphere in the ultraviolet (UV), visible (VIS) and near infrared (NIR) spectral ranges.  The ALTIUS instrument observes the ozone from side-on, at Earth’s limb, with a 1 km vertical resolution. This limb-sounding technique allows ozone to be viewed at different altitudes, thereby providing vertical profiles of different ozone concentrations, providing a 2D image of ozone in the atmosphere. In addition to nominal limb observations, the instrument will also perform solar and stellar occultation observations in the dark limb.  The channels that the instruments images in are provided:

Ultraviolet channel (UV) - 0.25 µm - 0.355 µm 

Visible channel (VIS) - 0.44 µm - 0.675 µm

Near Infrared Channel (NIR) - 0.6 µm - 1.02 µm"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ALTIUS"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Atmospheric Limb Tracker for the Investigation of the Upcoming Stratosphere"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.eoportal.org/satellite-missions/altius#sensorcomplement"@en ] .

