    skos:definition """The IGOR (Integrated GPS Occultation Receiver) of BRE (Broad Reach Engineering), Tempe, AZ, USA has been selected. The IGOR instrument, of BlackJack heritage, is customized to include a MIL-STD-1553B bus and two SSR (Solid State Recorders), each of 128 MByte. The IGOR instrument includes two RO antennas and two POD (Precision Orbit Determination) antennas. 37)

- IGOR instrument mass: 4.2 kg; size: 21.8 cm x 24.0 cm x 14.4 cm

- Peak power consumption: 25 W

- Tracking signals: L1 (1575.42 MHz) and L2 (1227.60 MHz)

- Tracking channels: 48 (4 antenna inputs)

- Sampling rate: 0.1 Hz and 50 Hz sampling; (0.1 Hz for POD support, 50 Hz for occultation science)"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "IGOR"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Integrated GPS Occultation Receiver"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Text Source: https://directory.eoportal.org/web/eoportal/satellite-missions/k/kompsat-5#sensors"@en ] .

