    skos:changeNote """2017-03-13 14:09:01.0 [mgenazzi] Definition added 
insert Definition (id: null
text: Scleractinia is a subclass of class Anthozoa (Phylum Cnidarian) of water-based organisms formed by colonial polyps with hexamerous symmetry, eight and ten part symmetry is not uncommon.  Stony corals, known as hard corals or 'reef-building corals, are sessile marine organisms that secrete a calicum carbonate skeleton to protect it's soft body.  Polyps are individual animals with a cylindrical body crowned by an oral disc and mouth surrounded by tentacles.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Scleractinia is a subclass of class Anthozoa (Phylum Cnidarian) of water-based organisms formed by colonial polyps with hexamerous symmetry, eight and ten part symmetry is not uncommon.  Stony corals, known as hard corals or 'reef-building corals, are sessile marine organisms that secrete a calicum carbonate skeleton to protect it's soft body.  Polyps are individual animals with a cylindrical body crowned by an oral disc and mouth surrounded by tentacles."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "HARD OR STONY CORALS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "encyclopedia of life"@en ] .

