    skos:definition "Phylum Gnathostomulida, commonly known as jaw worms, are marine microscopic free-living worms characterized by a monocliliated epidermis and complex cuticular mouthparts"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
