    skos:changeNote """2025-03-06 13:31:38.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Ultrafine Condensation Particle Counter is a types of condensation particle counter (CPC) is designed primarily for researchers interested in airborne particles smaller than 20 nm. It is a continuous-flow instrument that detects particles down to 2.5 nm. It uses a special sheath-air flow design that improves response to changes in particle concentration and increases counting efficiency for ultrafine particles.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Ultrafine Condensation Particle Counter is a types of condensation particle counter (CPC) is designed primarily for researchers interested in airborne particles smaller than 20 nm. It is a continuous-flow instrument that detects particles down to 2.5 nm. It uses a special sheath-air flow design that improves response to changes in particle concentration and increases counting efficiency for ultrafine particles."@en ;
