<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/e4ef69d0-d32f-4b6f-ae6f-103863473000> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d49b2313-2fb1-464c-a2f8-5ff5799344a7> ;
    skos:definition """[Source: National Space Science Data Center, http://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/nmc/experimentDisplay.do?id=1991-082A-06 ]

The primary function of this investigation is to detect nuclear debris from nuclear detonations. The advanced X-ray detector, SSB/X, consists of two nonscanning sensors, one of which looks to the left and the other to the right of the ground track. Each sensor is a set of CdTe detectors which sense X rays in the three energy bands, >60 keV, >150 keV, and >375 keV.


