    skos:definition """In April 1958 Lockheed corporation won a US Navy competition to find a replacement for the Navy's aging P2V Neptune series of long range antisubmarine warfare and maritime patrol aircraft. Lockheed's winning proposal was designated "P3V Orion". Named for the winter constellation of the mighty hunter, the Orion was actually derived from the famous Lockheed Electra civil airliner. 

[Text provided by:
http://www.geocities.com/lucktam/awacs/orion/orion.htm ]

[Photo provided by: 
http://www.farfromglory.com/images/p3b.jpg ]


Group: Platform_Details
   Entry_ID: P-3B ORION
   Group: Platform_Identification
      Platform_Category: Aircraft
      Short_Name: P-3B ORION
      Long_Name: Lockheed P-3B Orion
   End_Group
   Creation_Date: 2008-07-14
   Online_Resource: http://aeroweb.brooklyn.cuny.edu/specs/lockheed/p-3b.htm
   Online_Resource: http://www.aeroflight.co.uk/types/usa/lockheed_martin/p-3/P-3_Orion.htm
   Sample_Image: http://www.farfromglory.com/images/p3b.jpg
End_Group"""@en ;
