<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ed019e00-9b0a-4bdc-89aa-606cc929bd9f> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ea855d4c-f132-44f9-b31c-447e1101684d> ;
    skos:changeNote """2017-03-15 10:43:14.0 [mgenazzi] Definition added 
insert Definition (id: null
text: Phylum Chordata. Class Chondrichthyes. Elasmobranchii are cartilaginous fish characterized by having five to seven pairs of gill clefts, rigid dorsal fins and placoid scales. Sharks have pectoral fins not fused to their head. Chimaeras have soft bodies and a single gill-opening and primarily live in deep water. Rays are distinguished by their flattened bodies, enlarged pectoral fins fused to the head with gill openings on their ventral surface.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Phylum Chordata. Class Chondrichthyes. Elasmobranchii are cartilaginous fish characterized by having five to seven pairs of gill clefts, rigid dorsal fins and placoid scales. Sharks have pectoral fins not fused to their head. Chimaeras have soft bodies and a single gill-opening and primarily live in deep water. Rays are distinguished by their flattened bodies, enlarged pectoral fins fused to the head with gill openings on their ventral surface."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "SHARKS/RAYS/CHIMAERAS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "encyclopedia of life"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ed0501c5-310c-42ab-b1eb-66e211f22803> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/9246fc12-17e7-4473-b9c0-c23e4bfc4eda> ;
    skos:changeNote """2012-06-26 12:35:20.0 [gee-cee] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (PERMAFROST MELT [ed0501c5-310c-42ab-b1eb-66e211f22803,39881] - TERRESTRIAL HYDROSPHERE INDICATORS [9246fc12-17e7-4473-b9c0-c23e4bfc4eda,39869]); 
""",
        """2024-10-08 13:46:24.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Refers to the melt of permafrost. A thawing permafrost layer can lead to severe impacts on people and the environment. For instance, as ice-filled permafrost thaws, it can turn into a muddy slurry that cannot support the weight of the soil and vegetation above it. Infrastructure such as roads, buildings, and pipes could be damaged as permafrost thaws.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Refers to the melt of permafrost. A thawing permafrost layer can lead to severe impacts on people and the environment. For instance, as ice-filled permafrost thaws, it can turn into a muddy slurry that cannot support the weight of the soil and vegetation above it. Infrastructure such as roads, buildings, and pipes could be damaged as permafrost thaws."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PERMAFROST MELT"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://www.epa.gov/climate-indicators/climate-change-indicators-permafrost"@en ] .

