Advisory will incorporate information on geomagnetic storms that may interfere
with some technology, including satellite communications."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "GEOMAGNETIC STORM"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Space Studies Board, Commission on Physical Sciences, Mathematics, and\r
Applications National Research Council "http://www.nas.edu/ssb/glossary.html" \r
"http://www.geolab.nrcan.gc.ca/geomag/e_effects.html\""""@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ed5106fd-a73f-4203-87a3-9c9e7e85dcfc> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d46a5046-e1c6-4a09-a2f1-db6a21eda611> ;
    skos:definition """The HFCs are a class of replacements for CFCs. Because they do not\r
contain chlorine or bromine, they do not deplete the ozone layer. All HFCs\r
have an ozone depletion potential of 0. Some HFCs have high GWPs (Global\r
Warming Potentials). HFCs are numbered according to a standard scheme. The\r
National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) provides more\r
detailed information about HFCs on their  <A\r
HREF="http://www.cmdl.noaa.gov/noah/flask/hfc.html">web site</a>."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "HYDROFLUOROCARBONS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) Ozone Depletion Glossary at
"http://www.epa.gov/ozone/defns.html\""""@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ed567f43-a195-48ab-8a39-fb81e75e8a7a> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/e97d2b88-a545-4882-801b-40964a2bc723> ;
