    skos:definition """The Global Telecommunication System (GTS) consists of  an integrated network of point-to-point circuits, and multi-point circuits which interconnect meteorological telecommunication centres.

The circuits of the GTS are composed of a combination of terrestrial and satellite telecommunication 
links of:

- point-to-point circuits,
        
- point-to-multi-point circuits for data distribution,
       
- multi-point-to-point circuits for data collection,
        
- as well as data-communication network services. 

[Text and Photo Source, World Meteorological Organization: http://www.wmo.ch/pages/prog/www/TEM/GTS/gts.html ]


