text: Atmosphere-Space Interactions Monitor on the ISS
language code: en); 
""",
        """2021-08-17 17:36:41.0 [sritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: ASIM is a climate observatory designed for detecting transient luminous event and terrestrial gamma ray flashes. ASIM will be mounted externally on the European Space Laboratory on ISS, Columbus. The ASIM payload consists of four sub-systems, CEPA, DHPU, MXGS, and MMIA. The CEPA and DHPU form the structural and electrical platform servicing the MXGS and MMIA scientific instruments. The DHPU, MXGS, and MMIA are mounted on-top of the CEPA. The power and data connections from ISS are routed through the CEPA to the DHPU, which converts 120V ISS supply to 28V instrument supply and handles all data communication.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2021-08-17 17:38:04.0 [sritz]  
update Definition (ASIM Payload Homepage, https://www.asim.dk/payload.php); 
""",
