    skos:definition """Paleomagnetism is the study of natural remnant magnetization of the Earth's
materials in order to determine the itensity and direction of the Earth's
magnetic field in the geologic past. Variations in the Earth's magnetic field
can be used as a means of stratigraphic correlation. Major reversals of the
Earth's magnetic field are well known and the record of these reversals in
sediments can be used as time markers or chronostratigraphic horizons."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PALEOMAGNETIC DATA"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological
Institute.
Bradley, R.S. 1999. Paleoclimatology: Reconstructing Climates of the
Quaternary, 2nd edition. Harcourt Academic Press."""@en ] .

