text: The Wyoming Cloud Radar (WCR)  is a 95Ghz, dual-channel, Doppler Radar designed for airborne use.  The UW King Air installation of the WCR uses three antennas- one that can look either upward or horizontally (to the right of the aircraft) plus two downward--looking antennas  (one at nadir; the second slanted ~30 degrees forward of nadir along the aircraft centerline).
language code: en); 
""",
        """2013-06-17 10:28:02.0 [saritz] Added primary long name. 
insert AltLabel (id: null
text: Wyoming Cloud Radar
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Wyoming Cloud Radar (WCR)  is a 95Ghz, dual-channel, Doppler Radar designed for airborne use.  The UW King Air installation of the WCR uses three antennas- one that can look either upward or horizontally (to the right of the aircraft) plus two downward--looking antennas  (one at nadir; the second slanted ~30 degrees forward of nadir along the aircraft centerline)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
