        """2013-03-11 13:35:47.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The identification of isotopic signature, the distribution of certain stable isotopes and chemical elements within chemical compounds. This can be applied to a food web to make it possible to draw direct inferences regarding diet, trophic level, and subsistence. Isotope ratios are measured using mass spectrometry, which separates the different isotopes of an element on the basis of their mass-to-charge ratio.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The identification of isotopic signature, the distribution of certain stable isotopes and chemical elements within chemical compounds. This can be applied to a food web to make it possible to draw direct inferences regarding diet, trophic level, and subsistence. Isotope ratios are measured using mass spectrometry, which separates the different isotopes of an element on the basis of their mass-to-charge ratio."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ISOTOPE RATIOS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "National Academy of Sciences"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/f7a09d7f-59cd-495d-97ad-bc7a09a50b0d> a skos:Concept ;
