update PrefLabel (ATMOSPHERIC FEEDBACKS); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Processes within the atmosphere through which the climate system is
controlled, changed, or modulated. Atmospheric feedbacks involve a
perturbation in a climate quantity that causes a change in a second
quantity, and the change in the second quantity ultimately leads to an
additional change in the first. Examples include water vapor and cloud
feedbacks."""@en ;
