category: primary
text: DEWPOINT HYDROMETERS
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """DEWPOINT HYDROMETERS are instruments used for determining the
dewpoint (the temperature at which a given air parcel must be
cooled at constant pressure and constant water vapor in order
for saturation to occur); a small temperature sensor is embedded
on the underside of a mirror and the electro-optical system is
used to detect the formation of condensate or dew; specular
reflectance of the bare mirror decreases the dew layer
thickness."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
    skos:prefLabel "DEWPOINT HYDROMETERS"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "DEWPOINT HYDROMETERS"@en ] .

