<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3f45aadf-ec7c-43a1-a008-b24ca139837a> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/c7b5c02c-724d-4a19-b824-98180f3900c9> ;
    skos:changeNote """2020-01-02 14:28:14.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (PLANT PHENOLOGY [3f45aadf-ec7c-43a1-a008-b24ca139837a,84889] - GROWTH STAGE [0f18f64b-dfac-4f93-9ded-89c8f249c2d1,559603]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """The science that treats the periodic biological phenomena with relation to\r
climate, especially seasonal changes.\r
Phenological events are stages of plant growth. From a climatological\r
viewpoint, these phenomena serve as bases for the interpretation of progress in
local seasons and the climatic zones, and are considered to integrate the\r
effects of a number of bioclimatic factors on rate of plant development.\r
Phenology may be considered a branch of the science of bioclimatics, the\r
sequence of plant or crop development stages through its life cycle. Growth\r
stages may be defined by stage of physiological development such as\r
germination, first true leaf, flowering, maturity, etc., and/or by physical\r
stage such as planting, emergence, harvest, etc."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/0f18f64b-dfac-4f93-9ded-89c8f249c2d1> ;
    skos:prefLabel "PLANT PHENOLOGY"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text """From the American Meteorological Society (AMS) Glossary of Meteorology Online\r
"http://amsglossary.allenpress.com/glossary/\""""@en ] .

