""",
        """2013-03-11 12:34:20.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Hydrogen gas is colorless, odorless, tasteless, flammable, and nontoxic. Hydrogen gas exists as a gas at ambient temperatures and atmospheric pressures. Hydrogen gas is the lightest gas known with a density approximately 0.07 that of air. The concentration of hydrogen gas in the atmosphere volume is 5.0 x 10-5%. Hydrogen is principally shipped and used in gaseous form for refineries, petrochemical companies for hydrotreating, catalytic reforming and hydrocracking. Hydrogen is also used in heat treating, metal production, welding, lasers, plastics, food production, and semiconductors.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Hydrogen gas is colorless, odorless, tasteless, flammable, and nontoxic. Hydrogen gas exists as a gas at ambient temperatures and atmospheric pressures. Hydrogen gas is the lightest gas known with a density approximately 0.07 that of air. The concentration of hydrogen gas in the atmosphere volume is 5.0 x 10-5%. Hydrogen is principally shipped and used in gaseous form for refineries, petrochemical companies for hydrotreating, catalytic reforming and hydrocracking. Hydrogen is also used in heat treating, metal production, welding, lasers, plastics, food production, and semiconductors."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/833b6958-fc93-473c-aadb-bb65da7578e5> ;
    skos:prefLabel "HYDROGEN GAS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Spectra Gases Inc."@en ] .

