        """2013-03-20 16:58:39.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: "(Or lenticular cloud.) A cloud species the elements of which have the form of more or less isolated, generally smooth lenses or almonds; the outlines are sharp and sometimes show irisation.

These clouds appear most often in formations of orographic origin, the result of lee waves, in which cases they remain nearly stationary with respect to the terrain (standing cloud), but they also occur in regions without marked orography. This species is found mainly in the genera cirrocumulus, altocumulus, and (rarely) stratocumulus. Altocumulus lenticularis differs from cirrocumulus lenticularis in that, when smooth and without elements, it has shadowed parts while the latter is very white throughout. When undulated or subdivided, the altocumulus species differs from stratocumulus lenticularis in that its elements subtend an angle of less than 5° when viewed at an angle of more than 30° above the horizon.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2013-04-15 15:09:03.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (ALTOCUMULUS LENTICULARIS [dbc7fed3-ad30-4e57-868e-bae478713a71,87473] - LENTICULAR CLOUDS [d5e72d73-22f6-4f4c-b937-b71d84960a1e,105089]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """"(Or lenticular cloud.) A cloud species the elements of which have the form of more or less isolated, generally smooth lenses or almonds; the outlines are sharp and sometimes show irisation.

These clouds appear most often in formations of orographic origin, the result of lee waves, in which cases they remain nearly stationary with respect to the terrain (standing cloud), but they also occur in regions without marked orography. This species is found mainly in the genera cirrocumulus, altocumulus, and (rarely) stratocumulus. Altocumulus lenticularis differs from cirrocumulus lenticularis in that, when smooth and without elements, it has shadowed parts while the latter is very white throughout. When undulated or subdivided, the altocumulus species differs from stratocumulus lenticularis in that its elements subtend an angle of less than 5° when viewed at an angle of more than 30° above the horizon."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d5e72d73-22f6-4f4c-b937-b71d84960a1e> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ALTOCUMULUS LENTICULARIS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "American Meteorological Society (http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Main_Page)"@en ] .

<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/dc626ae7-1ebe-4b9d-9b73-c048fa92434f> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3466eed1-2fbb-49bf-ab0b-dc08731d502b> ;
    skos:changeNote """2020-06-18 16:43:21.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (Sentinel-5 [dc626ae7-1ebe-4b9d-9b73-c048fa92434f,560376] - Earth Observation Satellites [3466eed1-2fbb-49bf-ab0b-dc08731d502b,541501]); 
""",
        """2020-06-18 16:45:05.0 [mmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: SENTINEL-5 is a European Earth observation mission developed to support the European Commission Copernicus Programme for monitoring the earth.

 

The SENTINEL-5 mission consists in a single instrument which is a UV-VIS-NIR-SWIR spectrometer observing the earth in nadir mode with a wide swath. It is embarked as a Customer Furnished Item (CFI) on the MetOp-SG A satellite (illustrated in Figure 1) which is operated by EUMETSAT as part of the EPS-SG (EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation) system.

 

The main objective of the SENTINEL-5 mission is to perform atmospheric measurements, with high spatio-temporal resolution, relating to air quality, climate forcing, ozone and UV radiation and providing a daily global coverage.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2020-06-18 16:45:52.0 [mmorahan] Move Concepts 
add narrower relation (Sentinel-5 [dc626ae7-1ebe-4b9d-9b73-c048fa92434f,560376] - Sentinel-5P [77e9a75e-2c3b-428b-8b21-b6a902dd8fee,541991]); 
""",
        """2020-10-05 15:33:03.0 [mmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Copernicus: Sentinel-5
language code: en); 
""",
        """2021-11-18 12:42:09.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (Sentinel-5 [dc626ae7-1ebe-4b9d-9b73-c048fa92434f,826816] - Space-based Platforms [b39a69b4-c3b9-4a94-b296-bbbbe5e4c847,835875]); 
""",
        """2021-11-18 13:00:31.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (Sentinel-5 [dc626ae7-1ebe-4b9d-9b73-c048fa92434f,826816] - Earth Observation Satellites [3466eed1-2fbb-49bf-ab0b-dc08731d502b,826121]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """SENTINEL-5 is a European Earth observation mission developed to support the European Commission Copernicus Programme for monitoring the earth.

 

The SENTINEL-5 mission consists in a single instrument which is a UV-VIS-NIR-SWIR spectrometer observing the earth in nadir mode with a wide swath. It is embarked as a Customer Furnished Item (CFI) on the MetOp-SG A satellite (illustrated in Figure 1) which is operated by EUMETSAT as part of the EPS-SG (EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation) system.

 

The main objective of the SENTINEL-5 mission is to perform atmospheric measurements, with high spatio-temporal resolution, relating to air quality, climate forcing, ozone and UV radiation and providing a daily global coverage."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/platforms> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/77e9a75e-2c3b-428b-8b21-b6a902dd8fee> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sentinel-5"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Copernicus: Sentinel-5"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/missions/sentinel-5/overview"@en ] .

