    skos:changeNote """2022-03-03 17:49:15.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (HYDROCHLOROFLUOROCARBONS [f6b97280-74d0-4233-bd17-f9f3d9dd21c2,833689] - HCFC-22 [f2464ebf-811a-43c2-bd50-9e80e03e07b3,836069]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """HCFCs, with one or more hydrogen-carbon bonds  are slated to replace CFCs\r
in most of the current applications. HCFCs are more unstable and subject\r
to hydroxyl radical and  ozone attack early in their gas phase career in\r
the atmosphere. Therefore, their atmospheric lifetime is projected to be\r
shorter  and their chance of reaching the stratosphere\r
decreased. [Spectator; v 272; p 9-11; 1994][New Scientist; v 141; p 6-7;\r
1994.]"""@en ;
