        """2024-02-22 09:15:00.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Ribonucleic acid (abbreviated RNA) is a molecule present in all living cells that is transcribed from and has structural similarities to DNA. The “transcript” is the RNA produced when a gene is transcribed. Unlike DNA, RNA is most often single-stranded. Includes mRNA (messenger), tRNA (transfer), and rRNA (ribosomal).
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Ribonucleic acid (abbreviated RNA) is a molecule present in all living cells that is transcribed from and has structural similarities to DNA. The “transcript” is the RNA produced when a gene is transcribed. Unlike DNA, RNA is most often single-stranded. Includes mRNA (messenger), tRNA (transfer), and rRNA (ribosomal)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/7d3c1302-4d88-4964-b966-f318bf2bcf74>,
