""",
        """2024-12-13 12:35:46.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Joint Radiation Experiment includes CARMEN-3 and Light Particle Telescope (LPT), which are used to measure the satellite's space environment, particularly the effects of radiation and charged particles on advanced components. CARMEN-3 (Characterization and Modeling of Environment) measures charged particles fluxes and the effects of these fluxes on instruments in Jason-3's orbit environment. It includes a sensor that measures low-level ions and electrons.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Joint Radiation Experiment includes CARMEN-3 and Light Particle Telescope (LPT), which are used to measure the satellite's space environment, particularly the effects of radiation and charged particles on advanced components. CARMEN-3 (Characterization and Modeling of Environment) measures charged particles fluxes and the effects of these fluxes on instruments in Jason-3's orbit environment. It includes a sensor that measures low-level ions and electrons."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/instruments> ;
