    skos:definition """Amphibians are craniates with a permeable skin across which respiration\r
can take place.  Their life cycle includes a shell-less egg which gives\r
rise to a distinct larval form.  The amphibians are free living in fresh\r
water and on land (some are arboreal) but all are dependent on water or\r
damp conditions."""@en ;
