        """2024-10-09 10:18:39.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Low-level clumps or patches of cloud varying in color from bright white to dark grey. They are the most common clouds on earth recognized by their well-defined bases, with some parts often darker than others. They usually have gaps between them, but they can also be joined together.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "Low-level clumps or patches of cloud varying in color from bright white to dark grey. They are the most common clouds on earth recognized by their well-defined bases, with some parts often darker than others. They usually have gaps between them, but they can also be joined together."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5857260b-1de6-47c2-8f66-5c0dbac42e32>,
