    skos:definition "Geographical Information Systems (GIS) are defined as Data Analysis\r and Visualization Services that are designed specifically to process and\r visualize geographically referenced data in a layered format. Statistical\r or mathematical algorithms may or may not be applied to the data within\r the service, but would be done so (and the results displayed) in a\r graphical manner. EXAMPLES: Idrisi, Arc/Info."@en ;
