<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/b1337c5b-c705-42c0-bc07-97689734253c> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3466eed1-2fbb-49bf-ab0b-dc08731d502b> ;
    skos:changeNote """2020-10-05 09:51:24.0 [mmorahan]  
insert AltLabel (id: null
category: primary
text: Applications Explorer Mission
language code: en); 
""",
        """2020-10-05 09:53:54.0 [mmorahan]  
update AltLabel (Applications Explorer Mission (AEM)); 
""",
        """2021-12-02 08:45:52.0 [tstevens]  
update PrefLabel (Applications Explorer Mission (AEM)); 
""",
        """2022-02-28 08:12:53.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A planned series of space applications missions whose purpose is to perform various tasks that require a low cost, quick reaction, small spacecraft in a dedicated orbit. The Heat Capacity Mapping Mission (HCMM) is the first mission of this series. The spacecraft described in this document was conceived to support a variety of applications instruments and the HCMM instrument in particular. The maximum use of commonality has been achieved. That is, all of the subsystems employed are taken directly or modified from other programs such as IUE, IMP, RAE, and Nimbus. The result is a small versatile spacecraft. The purpose of this document, the AEM Mission Planners Handbook (AEM/MPH) is to describe the spacecraft and its capabilities in general and the HCMM in particular. This document will also serve as a guide for potential users as to the capabilities of the AEM spacecraft and its achievable orbits. It should enable each potential user to determine the suitability of the AEM concept to his mission.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "A planned series of space applications missions whose purpose is to perform various tasks that require a low cost, quick reaction, small spacecraft in a dedicated orbit. The Heat Capacity Mapping Mission (HCMM) is the first mission of this series. The spacecraft described in this document was conceived to support a variety of applications instruments and the HCMM instrument in particular. The maximum use of commonality has been achieved. That is, all of the subsystems employed are taken directly or modified from other programs such as IUE, IMP, RAE, and Nimbus. The result is a small versatile spacecraft. The purpose of this document, the AEM Mission Planners Handbook (AEM/MPH) is to describe the spacecraft and its capabilities in general and the HCMM in particular. This document will also serve as a guide for potential users as to the capabilities of the AEM spacecraft and its achievable orbits. It should enable each potential user to determine the suitability of the AEM concept to his mission."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/platforms> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/7921a2bb-f13b-43ce-ad18-cfce4f3deb9c>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a796345a-53d4-400d-ba32-e7c7eaa1a1cc>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/cb310a29-01bb-4b52-8ff2-52dbfda7d050> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Applications Explorer Mission (AEM)"@en ;
    gcmd:altLabel [ gcmd:category "primary"@en ;
            gcmd:text "Applications Explorer Mission (AEM)"@en ] ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19740019251"@en ] .

