<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/06180441-d4bb-4fed-b36a-9b3cb2cac0fe> ;
    skos:changeNote """2016-06-28 15:12:05.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - TROPICAL CYCLONES [06180441-d4bb-4fed-b36a-9b3cb2cac0fe,217775]); 
""",
        """2016-06-28 15:12:42.0 [saritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The atmospheric pressure at the center of a high or low.  It is the highest pressure in a high and the lowest pressure in a low, referring to the sea level pressure of the system.   In a hurricane, a lower central pressure create a stronger gradient from outside to inside the system.  The stronger this pressure gradient is, the greater the maximum wind speeds around the eye wall.
language code: en); 
""",
        """2016-07-31 20:05:03.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - HURRICANES  (N. ATLANTIC/E. PACIFIC) [3b1544bc-1711-4553-a643-5d8fba38a1f1,247561]); 
""",
        """2016-07-31 20:05:21.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - TYPHOONS (WESTERN N. PACIFIC) [cfb85bf2-9920-4e3f-bce3-3d8f68ab1436,247563]); 
""",
        """2016-07-31 20:05:40.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - SEVERE TROPICAL CYCLONES (SW PACIFIC/SE INDIAN) [5b70e02b-0ed2-42a0-9fe9-7a552d6819d1,247565]); 
""",
        """2016-07-31 20:05:53.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - SEVERE CYCLONIC STORMS (N. INDIAN) [50abff20-11a8-4aea-8425-c9a05b1d8d09,247567]); 
""",
        """2016-07-31 20:06:03.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - CYCLONES (SW INDIAN) [ef467c3c-0aed-4aa8-bfa5-67721e83e557,247569]); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The atmospheric pressure at the center of a high or low.  It is the highest pressure in a high and the lowest pressure in a low, referring to the sea level pressure of the system.   In a hurricane, a lower central pressure create a stronger gradient from outside to inside the system.  The stronger this pressure gradient is, the greater the maximum wind speeds around the eye wall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3b1544bc-1711-4553-a643-5d8fba38a1f1>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/50abff20-11a8-4aea-8425-c9a05b1d8d09>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5b70e02b-0ed2-42a0-9fe9-7a552d6819d1>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/cfb85bf2-9920-4e3f-bce3-3d8f68ab1436>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ef467c3c-0aed-4aa8-bfa5-67721e83e557> ;
    skos:prefLabel "MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "Southeast Coastal Ocean Observing Regional Association (SECOORA) Hurricane Glossary."@en ] .

