        """2021-12-02 08:53:58.0 [tstevens]  
update PrefLabel (Disaster Monitoring Constellation- 1st Generation (DMC-1G)); 
""",
        """2022-03-02 12:44:38.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Disaster Monitoring Constellation (DMC) is an international program initially proposed in 1996 and led by SSTL (Surrey Satellite Technology Ltd), Surrey, UK, to construct a network of five affordable LEO microsatellites. The objective is to provide a daily global imaging capability at medium resolution (30-40 m), in 3-4 spectral bands, for rapid-response disaster monitoring and mitigation.
language code: en); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "The Disaster Monitoring Constellation (DMC) is an international program initially proposed in 1996 and led by SSTL (Surrey Satellite Technology Ltd), Surrey, UK, to construct a network of five affordable LEO microsatellites. The objective is to provide a daily global imaging capability at medium resolution (30-40 m), in 3-4 spectral bands, for rapid-response disaster monitoring and mitigation."@en ;
