    skos:definition """A very short electromagnetic wave. The portion of the electromagnetic\r
spectrum lying between the far infrared and the conventional radio\r
frequency  portion. While not bounded by definition, it is commonly\r
regarded as  extending from 1 mm to 1 m in wavelength (300 GHz to 0.3 GHz\r
frequency).  <P> Passive systems operating at these wavelengths sometimes\r
are called  microwave systems. Active systems are called radar, although\r
the literal definition of radar requires a distance measuring capability\r
not always included in active systems."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
