<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Climate Feedback Loops"@en,
        "Climate Feedback Mechanisms"@en ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/23703b6b-ee15-4512-b5b2-f441547e2edf> ;
    skos:changeNote """2019-05-30 07:56:10.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (Climate Feedbacks [de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691,368851] - CLIMATE INDICATORS [23703b6b-ee15-4512-b5b2-f441547e2edf,86343]); 
""",
        """2019-05-30 08:19:49.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (Climate Feedbacks [de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691,368851] - Atmospheric Feedbacks [fc77777e-614f-41f1-9b97-d5324fa99105,368855]); 
""",
        """2019-05-30 08:20:27.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (Climate Feedbacks [de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691,368851] - Coupled System Feedbacks [6a6bed83-f95a-44e6-8ae0-1371b532abc3,368859]); 
""",
        """2019-05-30 08:26:25.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (Climate Feedbacks [de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691,368851] - Cryospheric Feedbacks [3da6855e-9be8-4a79-826e-4ce984ed49a5,368863]); 
""",
        """2019-05-30 08:26:41.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (Climate Feedbacks [de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691,368851] - Land-Surface Feedbacks [514c891b-60b8-4a6f-adb3-0366c75588e9,368867]); 
""",
        """2019-05-30 08:26:56.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (Climate Feedbacks [de62c07e-96c6-44fb-a3a1-cd2902305691,368851] - Oceanic Feedbacks [80d337f4-8e90-456a-9a5b-33e5f5c907ce,368871]); 
""",
        """2019-06-03 14:41:15.0 [mmorahan] Rename Concept 
update PrefLabel (CLIMATE FEEDBACKS); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """An interaction in which a perturbation in one climate quantity causes a
change in a second and the change in the second quantity ultimately
leads to an additional change in the first. A negative feedback is one in
which the initial perturbation is weakened by the changes it causes; a
positive feedback is one in which the initial perturbation is enhanced.
The initial perturbation can either be externally forced or arise as part of
internal variability."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3da6855e-9be8-4a79-826e-4ce984ed49a5>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/514c891b-60b8-4a6f-adb3-0366c75588e9>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/6a6bed83-f95a-44e6-8ae0-1371b532abc3>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/80d337f4-8e90-456a-9a5b-33e5f5c907ce>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/fc77777e-614f-41f1-9b97-d5324fa99105> ;
    skos:prefLabel "CLIMATE FEEDBACKS"@en ;
    gcmd:reference [ gcmd:text "IPCC Special Report: Global Warming of 1.5ºC Glossary: https://www.ipcc.ch/sr15/chapter/glossary/"@en ] .

