<https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/376a1d5c-2496-4381-981f-bc047af92044> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/fa0a36c3-2503-4662-98cd-7f3e74ce9f80> ;
    skos:changeNote """2024-10-03 09:02:22.0 [tstevens] Remove Concepts 
delete narrower relation (null); 
""" ;
    skos:definition """Soil within which the moisture has predominantly changed to ice, the unfrozen\r
portion being in vapor phase. \r
Ice within the soil bonds (adfreezes) adjacent soil particles and renders\r
frozen ground very hard. Permanently frozen ground is called permafrost. Dry\r
frozen ground is relatively loose and crumbly because of the lack of bonding\r
ice. Frozen ground is sometimes inadvisedly called frost or ground frost."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords> ;
    skos:narrower <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/021714ad-1cae-441c-bb6f-4be866a0f742>,
        <https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/0cd7a96f-46e1-4d86-93d0-9cbb6fda61e3>,
