    skos:definition """A theory of global tectonics in which the lithosphere is \r
divided into a number of plates whose pattern of horizontal movement is \r
that of torsionally rigid bodies that interact with one another at their \r
boundaries, causing seismic and tectonic activity along these boundaries."""@en ;
