generated by: null); 
""" ;
    skos:definition "\"Fluvial landforms\" are features on the Earth's surface produced by the action, i.e. erosion and deposition, of a stream or river and include such landforms as bars, levees, braided and meandering channels, and alluvial fans.  \"Fluvial processes\" are those processes included in the action of running water in a stream or river"@en ;
